      "title": "Montana State University",
      "description": "tag:jobs.montana.edu,2005:/postings/all_jobs Montana State University - Bozeman: All Jobs 2026-01-09T10:23:35-07:00 https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50071 2026-01-09T10:23:34-07:00 2026-01-09T10:23:35-07:00 Finance Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The Jake Jabs College of Business and Entrepreneurship offers a Bachelor of Science in Business, with a concentration in finance degree. To accomplish our mission, a significant portion of our teaching faculty should have professional experience in practicing financial management. We seek experienced finance professionals with the ability to teach in more than one area, including financial markets, commercial banking, real estate finance, insurance and risk management, personal finance, investments corporate finance, and derivative securities.</div> Jabs College of Business Instruct https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52625 2026-08-19T09:47:58-06:00 2026-08-19T09:47:59-06:00 Administrative Associate IV, Buffalo Nations <div>Join the Buffalo Nations Food Systems Initiative as our Business Operations Manager and play a vital role in supporting Indigenous-centered education, research, and community engagement. You will work closely with the Director, faculty, students, Indigenous knowledge keepers, and community partners to coordinate programs, manage fiscal operations, and support impactful events and field research. This is an opportunity to contribute meaningfully to culturally grounded programming in a collaborative, mission-driven environment.</div> Food Systems Nutrition & Kinesiolog https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49998 2026-01-07T09:57:15-07:00 2026-01-07T09:57:15-07:00 Design Drafting Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty for the Design Drafting program.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52082 2026-07-01T08:46:50-06:00 2026-07-01T08:46:51-06:00 Custodian I - Full Time (Applicant Pool) <div>Applications are being accepted for the custodial pool at MSU!<br><br>There are a variety of shifts in these departments across the campus:</div><ul><li>Culinary Services</li><li>Sports Facilities</li><li>Strand Union Building</li><li>University Student Housing</li><li>Facilities Services</li><li>Student Wellness Center</li></ul> Auxiliary Services Administration https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52785 2026-09-02T09:16:49-06:00 2026-09-02T09:16:50-06:00 Academic Success Coordinator - Gianforte School of Computing <div>Serves as the program coordinator for the undergraduate and graduate programs in the Gianforte School of Computing. In this role, this person may perform course scheduling duties for the entire department. This person may also work with advisors to facilitate course registration. Additionally, this person may serve as the primary coordinator to the graduate students within the department and is responsible for correspondence with potential students, offer and assignment letters, graduate office interactions and other graduate program concerns as required. This person supports the director and faculty with reporting data, search management and as liaison to other campus offices.</div> Gianforte School of Computing https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52736 2026-08-27T14:52:57-06:00 2026-08-27T14:52:59-06:00 Mechanic II or III <div><strong>MECHANIC II</strong> – In addition to Mechanic I duties and responsibilities (primarily responsible for major mechanical work on vehicles, trucks, trailers, implements, large and small equipment, and tools.), the Mechanic II is primarily charged with performing all major mechanical work on vehicles, trucks, trailers, implements, campus standby generators, large and small equipment and tools. Includes welding ferrous and non-ferrous metals, including fabrication of parts for vehicles and equipment. Participates in University Services Fleet and Equipment condition assessment.<br><br><strong>MECHANIC III</strong> – In addition to Mechanic II duties and responsibilities, the Mechanic III is primarily charged with performing all major mechanical work on mid to heavy trucks, diesel engines, tractors hydraulics and other specialty vehicles, equipment, and implements.</div> Facility Services https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50034 2026-01-07T16:37:20-07:00 2026-01-07T16:37:21-07:00 Native American Studies Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The Department of Native American Studies seeks instructors to teach Native American Studies courses on an as needed basis. The courses may be on-campus or online.</div> Native American Studies https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52448 2026-08-03T08:09:43-06:00 2026-08-03T08:09:44-06:00 Senior Technology Manager <div>The Senior Technology Manager reports to the Director of the Technology Transfer Office and acts with a high degree of autonomy to assist MSU researchers to identify, protect, and license intellectual property to industry, supporting the TTO core mission of translating MSU research to practice, to maximize its societal impact.</div> MSU Technology Transfer Office https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49974 2026-01-06T17:39:07-07:00 2026-01-06T17:39:07-07:00 Marketing Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty <div>The Jake Jabs College of Business and Entrepreneurship offers a Bachelor of Science in Business, with a concentration in marketing degree. Marketing courses are also taught in the M.S. in Innovation and Management graduate program. To accomplish our mission, a significant portion of our teaching faculty should have professional experience in practicing marketing. We seek experienced marketing professionals capable of teaching a variety of established courses within our curriculum. Candidates should review the specific course descriptions at <a href=\"https://catalog.montana.edu/coursedescriptions/bmkt/\"><strong>https://catalog.montana.edu/coursedescriptions/bmkt/</strong></a> to identify their potential teaching areas. Additionally, we are interested in candidates capable of developing coursework in contemporary and industry-relevant areas, such as social media marketing.</div> Jabs College of Business Instruct https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/51324 2026-04-29T14:14:58-06:00 2026-04-29T14:14:59-06:00 Police Officer Commissioned (non-certified) <div>A Police Officer Commissioned (non-certified) is a police officer candidate who does not currently hold a Montana, or an out-of-state equivalent, POST certificate. The successful candidate will attend the Montana Law Enforcement Academy Law Enforcement Officer Basic Course in Helena, MT, for three months.<br><br>Montana State University police officers provide a safe and secure environment for living and learning on the MSU Campus. MSUPD officers are responsible for protecting lives and property through proactive patrols and response to all crimes, emergencies and related calls for service within the University Police jurisdiction. MSUPD officers provide law enforcement skills to prevent and investigate violations of the law, University rules, and regulations, under the direction of a police sergeant.</div> University Police https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50111 2026-01-14T13:50:17-07:00 2026-01-14T13:50:18-07:00 COMX 111US Public Speaking Instructor Non-Tenure Track (Applicant Pool) <div>The University Studies Program seeks instructors to teach the following class depending on need and available funding: COMX 111US Introduction to Public Speaking</div> University Studies https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52647 2026-08-20T12:22:55-06:00 2026-08-20T12:22:56-06:00 Library Tech II <div>This position provides metadata expertise including establishing controlled vocabularies and assigning semantic topics for library collections, using appropriate schema, to ensure materials in all physical and digital forms are optimally accessible; refines and improves metadata for library collections based on search engine optimization best practices; and creates metadata records in a variety of databases, digital asset management systems, and other applications, using specialized software tools.</div> Library https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50001 2026-01-07T10:13:42-07:00 2026-01-07T10:13:42-07:00 Agricultural and Technology Education Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) Agricultural Education https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52177 2026-07-09T12:40:13-06:00 2026-07-09T12:40:14-06:00 Extension Agent - On Farm Irrigation - Flathead Reservation <div><strong>This position resides at the MSU Flathead Reservation Extension Office in Polson, Montana</strong><br><br>The primary duty for MSU Flathead Reservation Extension Faculty is to assess community needs, then develop, implement, and evaluate Extension programming to meet those needs. The main emphasis of the MSU Extension Flathead Reservation Irrigation Efficiency Agent position will be to provide technical assistance to irrigators and producers to more effectively use irrigation water to enhance the growth of forages, pasture, and field crops. It is anticipated that the effective development and delivery of Extension programming will generate positive economic and community development impacts. This position will have a strong partnership with the Compact Implementation Technical Team (CITT), the interagency advisory committee implementing the CSKT-Montana Water Compact.<br><br>The MSU Flathead Reservation Extension Office currently has two other agents working in Extension disciplines. One agent position works in family and consumer sciences, youth development, and community mental health. The second agent works in the areas of agriculture and horticulture. The office also houses two SNAP nutrition Agents.</div> Extension Agents/Field https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52797 2026-09-03T11:53:06-06:00 2026-09-03T11:53:07-06:00 Research Associate *Kalispell, MT* <div>Montana State University’s Northwestern Agricultural Research Center (NWARC) is seeking a motivated and detail-oriented individual to support its field crop physiology research program. This role offers a unique opportunity to contribute to applied agricultural research that directly benefits farmers and agribusinesses in Northwest Montana. The successful candidate will be involved in hands-on research across a variety of agronomic crops, helping to advance studies related to irrigation, nutrient management, and crop performance. The position combines fieldwork, data collection, and equipment operation with responsibilities in data management and seasonal staff supervision. Ideal candidates will have a strong foundation in agronomy or a related field, enjoy working outdoors, and be eager to collaborate with researchers, producers, and stakeholders to support MSU’s mission of agricultural innovation and outreach.</div> AES NWARC https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/51504 2026-05-14T11:46:27-06:00 2026-05-14T11:46:27-06:00 NAGPRA Program Lead <div>The NAGPRA Program Leadcoordinates compliance, consultations, repatriations, and other activities associated with ensuring MSU’s compliance with the Native American Graves Protection and Repatriation Act (NAGPRA) federal regulation by coordinating inventory and curation of Native American artifacts and remains. This position will work to strengthen MSU’s NAGPRA program and will report directly to the Associate Vice President of Research Compliance.</div> Research Integrity and Compliance https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52746 2026-08-28T15:32:55-06:00 2026-08-28T15:32:56-06:00 Training and Development Specialist <div>MSU Access and Success is seeking a Training and Development Specialist to support campus-wide initiatives that foster inclusive dialogue, effective communication, and community engagement. This position plays a key role in developing and delivering educational programming that enhances the ability of students, faculty, and staff to engage across differences and contribute to a welcoming and inclusive campus environment.<br><br></div><div>The Training and Development Specialist manages several signature programs, including Safe Zone, and Cultural Bridges, and collaborates with campus partners to expand training capacity and impact.<br><br></div><div>The Training and Development Specialist is responsible for the design, implementation, and continuous improvement of educational programs that support dialogue across differences, inclusive practices, and community engagement. This position manages key training initiatives and collaborates with campus partners to expand learning opportunities that foster effective communication, cultural awareness, and inclusive excellence.</div> DISC https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50036 2026-01-07T16:43:57-07:00 2026-01-07T16:43:58-07:00 Chinese Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>Department of Modern Languages and Literatures maintains an applicant pool for Non-Tenure Track Instructors in Chinese. Instructors typically teach 1 to 5 classes per semester. All positions are pending adequate enrollment and funding. This advertisement is for an applicant pool. It does not indicate whether or not there are any current openings. Qualified candidates will be contacted in the event a position opens.</div> Modern Languages & Literature https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52484 2026-08-04T16:53:09-06:00 2026-08-04T16:53:10-06:00 Executive Director, QCORE <div>QCORE seeks a strategic leader to build and sustain an organization that advances research and scientific discovery.</div> Physics https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49982 2026-01-07T09:54:21-07:00 2026-01-07T09:54:22-07:00 Construction Trades Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty for Construction Trades programs including HVAC-R, General Construction, and Plumbing.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52813 2026-09-03T15:47:25-06:00 2026-09-03T15:47:26-06:00 Laborer <div>Under general supervision of the Campus Maintenance Manager, the Laborer provides services to the University by performing, assisting and supporting the maintenance and care of buildings, grounds, equipment, and utilities.</div> Facility Services https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/26751 2021-10-20T16:49:19-06:00 2021-10-20T16:49:20-06:00 Ecology Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>Our instructors teach courses to students that are focusing their education on Fish and Wildlife Management, Conservation Biology, Organismal Biology and Biological Sciences Education. Most courses taught in the department involve field trip components in the Greater Yellowstone Eco-system. The Ecology Department comprises the largest student population within MSU's College of Letters and Sciences.</div> Ecology https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50288 2026-02-02T12:49:16-07:00 2026-02-02T12:49:17-07:00 Mechanical & Industrial Engineering Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>Mechanical &amp; Industrial Engineering faculty members are expected to contribute to excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching in areas of mechanical engineering, mechanical engineering technology or industrial engineering related to the applicant’s strengths. Other responsibilities include advising and mentoring undergraduate students, participation in accreditation activities and committee assignments, and service to the university, state, and profession.</div> Mechanical & Industrial Engineering https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52684 2026-08-25T08:22:27-06:00 2026-08-25T08:22:28-06:00 Director of Budget and Finance <div>Montana State University Student Wellness is seeking a Director of Budget and Finance to provide strategic leadership in financial planning and budget management for Student Wellness units including Campus Recreation, Counseling and Psychological Services, Student Health Services, and the broader SW enterprise. They will serve as the financial expert within Student Wellness, advising unit leads on the availability of funding for personnel and operational changes. The position will be physically located in the new Student Wellness Center, a 165,000 square foot facility that opened in August 2024. The new facility enhances the integrated and holistic model of student health and wellbeing at MSU. The Director of Budget and Finance is an important part of the SW team and critical to supporting the vision of building a thriving campus culture of health and wellbeing.</div> SWC AVP OPs https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50003 2026-01-07T11:38:18-07:00 2026-01-07T11:38:18-07:00 Civil Engineering Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>Civil Engineering faculty members contribute to excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching, advise and mentor undergraduate students, participate in college activities and committee assignments, and provide service to the University, State, and profession.<br><br>The Civil Engineering Department is seeking professionals to serve as Instructors in the following areas:</div><ul><li>Basic Civil/Construction Engineering</li><li>Cold Regions Engineering</li><li>Construction Engineering</li><li>Engineering Graphics</li><li>Environmental Engineering</li><li>Engineering Mechanics</li><li>Geotechnical Engineering</li><li>Hydraulics</li><li>Hydrology</li><li>Capstone Design</li><li>Structural Engineering</li><li>Surveying</li><li>Transportation Engineering</li><li>Engineering Economics</li><li>Professional Practice</li></ul> Civil Engineering https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52199 2026-07-10T13:49:46-06:00 2026-07-10T13:49:47-06:00 Pharmacy Technician <div>Join a mission-driven healthcare team dedicated to MSU student well-being. The SHS Pharmacy Technician plays a key role in delivering accurate, confidential, and accessible pharmacy services to MSU students from a state-of-the-art campus facility.</div> SWC Pharmacy https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49984 2026-01-07T09:54:31-07:00 2026-01-07T09:54:32-07:00 Networking/Cyber Security Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty for the Networking/Cyber Security programs.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/51628 2026-05-26T15:39:10-06:00 2026-05-26T15:39:11-06:00 Postdoctoral Researcher – Political Science and Systems Engineering <div>Join an interdisciplinary postdoctoral fellowship at Montana State University, in collaboration with engineering and political science faculty, to implement an existing research program defined in the DigiCARES strategic plan that advances justice-enhanced resilience in next-generation energy system digital twins. The position offers hands-on research using real-world utility data and community partners to support an equitable, data-driven energy transformation.</div> Political Science https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52751 2026-08-31T09:20:16-06:00 2026-08-31T09:20:17-06:00 Major Gifts Program Manager <div>The Major Gifts Program Manager at Museum of the Rockies is responsible for building, soliciting, and stewarding relationships with donors capable of making gifts of $10,000 or more. The position manages a portfolio of 70-100 donors and prospects, primarily in the Bozeman area, and is expected to meet fundraising goals that support the museum's annual operations, capital projects, exhibitions, and strategic initiatives.<br><br></div><div>Using a moves management approach, the Major Gifts Program Manager develops donor relationships through personal meetings and other forms of communication. They maintain accurate records and follow-up activities in the museum's donor database.<br><br></div><div>The ideal candidate is a self-motivated relationship builder with strong organizational, communication, and time-management skills, high personal integrity, and a proven ability to manage a donor portfolio and achieve revenue goals. An appreciation for the role of public institutions and museums is important. Some regional travel and occasional evening or weekend work are required.<br><br></div><div>The position reports to the Director of Development and Membership.</div> Museum of the Rockies https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50038 2026-01-07T16:48:56-07:00 2026-01-07T16:48:56-07:00 Japanese Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>Department of Modern Languages and Literatures maintains an applicant pool for Non-Tenure Track Instructors in Japanese. Instructors typically teach 1 to 5 language classes per semester. All positions are pending adequate enrollment and funding. This advertisement is for an applicant pool. It does not indicate whether or not there are any current openings. Qualified candidates will be contacted in the event a position comes open.</div> Modern Languages & Literature https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52506 2026-08-06T08:33:01-06:00 2026-08-06T08:33:02-06:00 Extension Agent - Fallon County <div>The primary duty for County Extension Faculty is to assess local community needs, then to develop, implement, and evaluate Extension programming to meet those needs. The primary emphasis for this full-time position will be to provide leadership and educational programming in the disciplines of 4-H/Youth Development, Agriculture, Natural Resources and Horticulture.<br><br></div><div>The Extension Office staff in Fallon County also includes a full-time office administrative assistant.</div> Extension Agents/Field https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52820 2026-09-03T16:32:05-06:00 2026-09-03T16:32:06-06:00 Director of Graduate Recruitment and Admissions <div>Join the Graduate School team to lead MSU’s graduate recruitment and admissions strategy, shaping the journey from prospect to enrollment. This role drives a dynamic, centralized approach to application processing, evaluation, and decision-making while enhancing the graduate student experience through impactful orientation programs. As a key partner to academic departments, the Director plays a pivotal role in attracting top talent and elevating MSU’s graduate community.</div> Graduate School https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49915 2026-01-02T14:19:26-07:00 2026-01-02T14:19:27-07:00 Continuing and Professional Education Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>Academic Technology and Outreach seeks non-tenure track faculty to teach non-credit courses in professional and personal development areas to include personal/professional finances, business leadership and development, science, technology, health and wellness, humanities, arts, and more. Instruction may take place in-person, online or in hybrid formats. Appointments are available throughout the academic year and summer. All positions are pending adequate course enrollment.</div> Extended University https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50723 2026-03-13T09:52:51-06:00 2026-03-13T09:52:51-06:00 Gen Ed - Workforce Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty for general education courses for the workforce programs.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52690 2026-08-25T09:05:37-06:00 2026-08-25T09:05:38-06:00 Civil Rights Investigator <div>Montana State University is seeking applications to fill one full-time Civil Rights Investigator position in Campus Civil Rights. As a member of the CCR team, the Civil Rights Investigator will support the University’s strategic plan and commitment to removing barriers to accessing University programs and services. The Civil Rights Investigator primarily supports the institutional commitment to civil rights compliance by conducting prompt and equitable resolutions through formal and informal means. The successful candidate will assist in outreach and engagement with and for the University community related to CCR’s jurisdiction and scope of work.</div> Campus Civil Rights https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50006 2026-01-07T12:05:44-07:00 2026-01-07T12:05:45-07:00 Electrical & Computer Engineering Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The Electrical &amp; Computer Engineering Department is seeking professionals to serve as Instructors in the following areas:<br><br>• Circuit Analysis and Design<br>• Communications Systems<br>• Control Systems<br>• Digital Systems<br>• Electromagnetics<br>• Electronics Materials<br>• Energy and Power Systems<br>• Engineering Design<br>• FPGA-based Embedded Systems<br>• Lasers &amp; Electro-optics<br>• Microfabrication<br>• Microprocessor-based Embedded Systems<br>• VLSI Design</div> Electrical Engineering https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52272 2026-07-16T16:47:13-06:00 2026-07-16T16:47:13-06:00 Political Science Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>Instructor to teach courses in political science open sub-fields including but not limited to American Politics, Political Theory, Public Administration and Policy, International Relations, Research Methods.</div> Political Science https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49986 2026-01-07T09:54:45-07:00 2026-01-07T09:54:45-07:00 Allied Health Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty for the Medical Assisting and Health Information programs.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/51689 2026-06-02T10:02:52-06:00 2026-06-02T10:02:53-06:00 Global Health Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>Housed in the Liberal Studies program, the Global Health minor allows students to develop an interdisciplinary understanding of health issues and health care in a global context. Through studying a broad range range of courses, this minor will be provided with a solid foundation in social, cultural, epidemiological, environmental, and nutritional determinants of health, and will explore the challenges that require global health solutions. The Liberal Studies Program seeks pool applications for potential instructors for Global Health courses such as LS 104: Intro to Global Health. These courses are regularly taught in the fall and spring semesters.</div> Liberal Studies https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52757 2026-08-31T11:03:26-06:00 2026-08-31T11:03:27-06:00 Dishwasher - Full-TIme (Applicant Pool) <div>MSU’s Culinary Services hires motivated team members who are excited to actively participate in the ever changing world of the high-paced food industry.</div> Culinary Services Administration https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50040 2026-01-07T16:52:07-07:00 2026-01-07T16:52:08-07:00 French Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>Department of Modern Languages and Literatures maintains an applicant pool for Non-Tenure Track Instructors in French. Instructors typically teach 1 to 5 language classes per semester. All positions are pending adequate enrollment and funding. This advertisement is for an applicant pool. It does not indicate whether or not there are any current openings. Qualified candidates will be contacted in the event a position comes open.</div> Modern Languages & Literature https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52524 2026-08-07T10:28:54-06:00 2026-08-07T10:28:55-06:00 Budget and Fiscal Manager <div>The Budget and Fiscal Manager for the Graduate School works collaboratively with Graduate School staff and university partners to support graduate student success. Reporting to the Vice Provost of Graduate Education, this position provides leadership and oversight for all fiscal operations, including budgeting, financial planning and analysis, fund management, policy implementation, and financial reporting.<br><br>The position oversees Graduate School budgets and expenditures, including tuition waivers, fellowships, completion awards, and travel awards, while supporting strategic initiatives and ensuring sound fiscal stewardship. Other duties may be assigned in support of the Graduate School's administrative operations.</div> Graduate School https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52289 2026-07-20T13:17:32-06:00 2026-07-20T13:17:33-06:00 Software Engineer <div>In support of the Montana State University mission, University Information Technology (UIT) promotes, develops, delivers, and facilitates the use of information technology services and resources.<br><br>This position is located in the Enterprise Services Group (ESG). ESG is responsible for technical support of all major computer-based administrative applications for the four-campus MSU system. MSU utilizes many hosted applications and third-party applications as well as Ellucian Banner software, running on an Oracle database. Modules include Human Resources (HR), Finance, Student, and Financial Aid. All modules are supported by a database/systems administration team. The Computer Software Engineer fills a vital role performing professional level work analyzing business needs and user requirements and designing and developing computer programs and user interfaces to meet those requirements.<br><br>This position provides technical support in testing, troubleshooting, and problem resolution for enterprise systems used by MSU. This position works closely with technical peers in the UIT ESG, and throughout UIT and MSU. This position is located in Bozeman and requires a limited amount of travel.</div> UIT Enterprise Services Group CUF https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52824 2026-09-03T16:43:49-06:00 2026-09-03T16:43:50-06:00 Research Associate – Pulse Crop Survey Program <div>This position will work under the supervision of the Associate Professor of Plant Pathology at the Eastern Agricultural Research Center to coordinate and conduct a regional pulse crop pest and disease survey program. Responsibilities include surveying commercial fields, collecting and managing field data, communicating findings with producers and agricultural stakeholders, supporting outreach activities and applied research that improve pest and disease management in Montana. The position serves as a link between agricultural producers, researchers, and other stakeholders by providing timely pest and disease information that supports management decisions and future research priorities. Training will be provided for program-specific survey protocols, ArcGIS Survey123, drone operations, and communication platforms.<br><br></div><div>This position provides a unique opportunity to help build and shape a growing regional pest and disease survey program while developing a broad range of skills in applied plant pathology, integrated pest management, agricultural technology, data management, and science communication. The successful candidate will work directly with Montana producers, agricultural professionals, and university researchers and will have opportunities to take increasing responsibility for program development, stakeholder engagement, applied research, and future expansion. We encourage candidates at different stages of their careers to apply. Whether you are beginning your career or bringing substantial experience in plant pathology, agriculture, or a related field, this position offers opportunities to develop new skills, contribute to a growing program, and take on increasing responsibility.</div> AES EARC https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49941 2026-01-06T13:25:25-07:00 2026-01-06T13:25:26-07:00 Instructor of Music Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The School of Music seeks qualified individuals to provide non-tenurable instruction in the following areas: applied music instruction, ensemble conducting, music theory, aural skills, keyboard skills, popular music, world music, music history, composition, music technology, and electroacoustic music.</div> Music https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50725 2026-03-13T09:54:49-06:00 2026-03-13T09:54:50-06:00 Gen Ed - Natural Sciences Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks Natural Science non-tenure track faculty for the AA/AS program.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52702 2026-08-25T13:35:17-06:00 2026-08-25T13:35:18-06:00 Program Coordinator II– Health Professions Resource Center <div>The full-time Student Success Coordinator provides a high level of customer service and student support to the office of Health Professions Resource Center.</div> University Studies https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50009 2026-01-07T12:15:42-07:00 2026-01-07T12:15:42-07:00 Chemical & Biological Engineering Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The Chemical &amp; Biological Engineering Department offers bachelor's degrees in chemical engineering as well as biological engineering. The Department is seeking professionals to serve as instructors in the following areas:<br><br></div><ul><li>Material Science</li><li>Material and Energy Balances</li><li>Unit Operations Laboratory</li><li>Fluid Mechanics</li><li>Thermodynamics</li><li>Heat Transfer</li><li>Separation Processes</li><li>Chemical Reaction Engineering</li><li>Process Dynamics and Control</li><li>Bioprocess Engineering</li><li>Bioseparations</li><li>Transport</li><li>Biotransport</li><li>Design (capstone design course)</li></ul><div><br>In addition, opportunities exist for teaching courses within our new biomedical engineering program, developing new courses, and teaching at the graduate level.</div> Chemical & Biological Engineering https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49988 2026-01-07T09:54:55-07:00 2026-01-07T09:54:56-07:00 Developmental Writing Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty to teach Basic Writing Skills (WRIT 080), Developmental Writing (WRIT 095), College Writing (WRIT 101) and Effective Academic Practices (COLS 100) to MSU and Gallatin College students.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/51827 2026-06-10T14:52:49-06:00 2026-06-10T14:52:50-06:00 Sous Chef <div>Culinary Services is looking for motivated team members who are excited to actively participate in the ever changing world of the high-paced food industry.</div> Miller Dining Commons https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52765 2026-08-31T14:39:58-06:00 2026-08-31T14:39:59-06:00 Custodial Supervisor II Residence Life Administration https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50042 2026-01-07T16:56:56-07:00 2026-01-07T16:56:57-07:00 Liberal Studies Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>Montana State University’s Liberal Studies program, located in the College of Letters &amp; Science, provides undergraduate students with a broad, integrated, and interdisciplinary learning experience. The Liberal Studies program seeks pool applications for potential instructors typically for LS 101 and/or LS 301. These courses are regularly taught in the fall and spring semesters.</div> Liberal Studies https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52581 2026-08-13T13:25:28-06:00 2026-08-13T13:25:29-06:00 Extension Agent – Agriculture and 4-H Youth Development – Pondera County <div>This position is located in <strong>Conrad, Montana.<br></strong><br></div><div>The primary duty for County Extension Faculty is to assess local community needs, then to develop, implement, and evaluate Extension programming to meet those needs. The primary emphases of the Pondera County Extension Agent position are in the areas of Agriculture and 4-H Youth Development, with secondary emphasis on Community Vitality. The Pondera County Extension office is staffed by a Family and Consumer Sciences and 4-H Youth Development agent, an Agriculture and 4-H Youth Development agent, and one full-time administrative assistant.</div> Extension Agents/Field https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50012 2026-01-07T12:33:24-07:00 2026-01-07T12:33:24-07:00 Women’s Gender and Sexuality Studies Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The Women’s Gender and Sexuality Studies program seeks non-tenure track instructors to teach upper and lower-level courses during the academic year.</div> Women's and Gender Studies https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52317 2026-07-21T10:21:49-06:00 2026-07-21T10:21:50-06:00 Visiting Scholar - Architecture (Non-Tenure Track Faculty Applicant Pool) <div>This one-semester position is intended to attract and support an emerging scholar or practitioner (or a group of scholars or practitioners) with a range of innovative scholarship or progressive practice in architecture or allied fields. Candidates are expected to teach, conduct research, and facilitate creative activity that will contribute to or challenge thinking about architecture as the School of Architecture looks to the future. A broad range of scholarly and professional expertise is welcomed.</div> Architecture https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52834 2026-09-04T09:11:44-06:00 2026-09-04T09:11:45-06:00 Parking Enforcement Officer I <div>Under the supervision of the Parking Enforcement Supervisor, Parking Enforcement Officers conduct foot and vehicle patrols of University parking lots in order to enforce campus parking regulations. Some of the duties will include: patrolling campus parking areas; issuing citations; use the T2 enforcement and parking management software; selling vehicle parking permits; providing information about the University to visitors; routinely work overtime assignments to assist with parking for special and athletic events; and assisting motorists in distress.</div> Parking Facility https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49943 2026-01-06T13:41:56-07:00 2026-01-06T13:41:57-07:00 Instructor of Film Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The School of Film &amp; Photography seeks qualified individuals to provide non-tenurable instruction in the following areas in the School’s Film Option: film and related media studies, film and video production (all aspects), film industry, acting, directing, scriptwriting, production management, science communication, wildlife and nature filmmaking, and digital media.</div> School of Film and Photography https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50897 2026-03-26T16:49:42-06:00 2026-03-26T16:49:42-06:00 Earth Sciences Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The Department of Earth Sciences at Montana State University seeks Non-Tenure Track Faculty to teach various Earth Sciences courses to undergraduate and graduate students.</div> Earth Sciences https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52711 2026-08-25T15:46:04-06:00 2026-08-25T15:46:05-06:00 Assistant Professor of Computer Science <div>The Gianforte School of Computing invites applications for multiple full-time tenure-track positions at the level of Assistant Professor. Primary responsibilities include developing a nationally recognized, externally funded research program, teaching both undergraduate and graduate courses consistent with the candidate’s background, and participating in professional/service activities.</div> Gianforte School of Computing https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52592 2026-08-14T11:23:58-06:00 2026-08-14T11:23:59-06:00 Turtle Island Tales Program Coordinator I <div><em>Turtle Island Tales</em> is looking for a dynamic and motivated individual to provide program coordination and administrative support to the research team and students dedicated to supporting well-being for Native American families and communities.</div> American Indian Rural Health Equity https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49993 2026-01-07T09:55:16-07:00 2026-01-07T09:55:16-07:00 CNC Machine Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty for the CNC Machining program.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/51961 2026-06-22T15:11:44-06:00 2026-06-22T15:11:45-06:00 Academic/Student Success Advisor <div>This position is responsible for the Advising, Student Services, Career Services and Academic Success of Gallatin College programs provided to both AA/AS and Workforce Students at both the primarily Gallatin College “East” location and the MSU Campus.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52772 2026-09-01T09:28:03-06:00 2026-09-01T09:28:04-06:00 Extension Agent – 4-H Youth Development – Lewis and Clark County <div>This position is located in <strong>Helena, Montana.</strong></div><div><br></div><div>The primary duty for County Extension Faculty is to assess local community needs, then to develop, implement, and evaluate Extension programming to meet those needs. The primary emphasis of the Lewis and Clark County 4-H Youth Development Extension Agent position is in the area of 4-H Youth Development.<em> </em>The Lewis and Clark County Extension office is staffed by an Agriculture/Horticulture Agent, Family and Consumer Science and Community Vitality Agent, and a full-time administrative professional.</div> Extension Agents/Field https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50046 2026-01-07T17:11:35-07:00 2026-01-07T17:11:35-07:00 Cooperative Veterinary Medicine Program Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) Veterinary Medicine WIMU https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50027 2026-01-07T15:47:35-07:00 2026-01-07T15:47:37-07:00 CLS Seminar Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The College of Letters and Sciences CLS Seminar Program is now accepting applications from those with demonstrated and effective teaching experience, to serve as teaching faculty in our CLS courses. Successful candidates will enjoy facilitating discussion on a variety of texts and topics and can exemplify expert learning in an exciting, multi-disciplinary seminar.</div> CLS Seminar https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52389 2026-07-27T13:24:12-06:00 2026-07-27T13:24:13-06:00 Cook III (Applicant Pool) <div>MSU's Culinary Services hires motivated team members who are excited to actively participate in the ever changing world of the fast-paced food industry.</div> Culinary Services Administration https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52837 2026-09-04T10:27:40-06:00 2026-09-04T10:27:41-06:00 Customer Experience Coordinator <div>The Parking Experience Coordinator serves as the primary customer service representative for MSU’s University Police - Parking and Transportation Services and is often the first point of contact for students, employees, campus visitors, and community members. This position provides customer support related to parking permits, citations, appeals, parking regulations, and account transactions while supporting the daily operations of Parking and Transportation Services.</div> Parking Facility https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49959 2026-01-06T16:25:20-07:00 2026-01-06T16:25:20-07:00 Activity Class for Credit Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The Activity Class for Credit (ACT) program is run through the <a href=\"https://www.montana.edu/fsnk/\"><strong>Food System and Kinesiology Department</strong></a> at MSU. We are recruiting Non-Tenure Track instructors for ACT courses. We offer a wide range of courses, some of which include yoga, soccer, basketball, weights. All positions are pending adequate enrollment and funding.</div> Food Systems Nutrition & Kinesiolog https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50977 2026-04-01T10:41:46-06:00 2026-04-01T10:41:46-06:00 Philosophy Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The Department of History and Philosophy seeks course instructors in the disciplines of philosophy on an as needed basis.</div> History and Philosophy https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52714 2026-08-25T16:16:54-06:00 2026-08-25T16:16:55-06:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate <div>The Neufeldt Lab is looking for a motivated postdoc to complete a federally funded chemistry research project.</div> Chemistry https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52607 2026-08-17T12:19:32-06:00 2026-08-17T12:19:34-06:00 Registered Dietitian Nutritionist <div>The Registered Dietitian Nutritionist (RDN) for Bobcat Athletics will assist 15 NCAA Division 1 sports programs and rodeo and spirit squad programs to provide nutrition counseling and medical nutrition therapy to individual student athletes, teams and coaches. This position reports directly to the Senior Associate Athletic Director for Student Services.</div> Athletics https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49995 2026-01-07T09:56:39-07:00 2026-01-07T09:56:40-07:00 Bookkeeping and Business Management Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty for the Bookkeeping and Business Management program.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52040 2026-06-29T14:22:47-06:00 2026-06-29T14:22:47-06:00 College of Nursing Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>Non-Tenure Track (NTT) faculty in the Mark and Robyn Jones College of Nursing teach undergraduate and/or graduate nursing courses using multiple teaching strategies including in-person active learning pedagogies, simulation learning, online/web-supported strategies, and/or clinical instruction. NTT faculty are located on one of the five CON campus sites (Bozeman, Billings, Great Falls, Kalispell, and Missoula) and participate in all aspects of the faculty teaching role. NTT faculty contribute to curriculum development, assessment, and continuous quality improvement. NTT faculty work collaboratively with other faculty and staff to develop cooperative relationships with clinical agencies, practitioners, and members of other disciplines to foster cutting-edge clinical education partnerships. NTT faculty report to a Campus Director.</div> Nursing Departments https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52777 2026-09-01T11:39:50-06:00 2026-09-01T11:39:51-06:00 Lead Systems Analyst <div>Lead the Enterprise Service Group (ESG) Finance team to support the four-campus Banner Finance operations. Collaborate with business counterparts to establish project priorities, address reported issues, and maintain existing processes.</div> UIT Enterprise Services Group CUF https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50049 2026-01-08T08:44:53-07:00 2026-01-08T08:44:53-07:00 NTT Faculty Instructors for MCB/MMLS College of Ag (Applicant Pool) Microbiology & Cell Biology https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50030 2026-01-07T15:55:05-07:00 2026-01-07T15:55:05-07:00 College Writing Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The MSU English Department maintains a pool of non-tenure-track applicants for consideration as potential instructors in writing courses.</div> English https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52423 2026-07-29T13:37:59-06:00 2026-07-29T13:38:00-06:00 Cook II (Applicant Pool) <div>MSU's Culinary Services hires motivated team members who are excited to actively participate in the ever changing world of the high-paced food industry.</div> Culinary Services Administration https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52839 2026-09-04T12:57:46-06:00 2026-09-04T12:57:47-06:00 Senior Employee Relations Specialist <div>Step into a critical, high-impact role at Montana State University as our Employee Relations Specialist, where your investigative expertise will directly drive the resolution of complex workplace challenges. We are seeking a principled professional to navigate sensitive personnel matters head-on, ensuring fair, compliant, and consistent practices through objective analysis and strategic leadership guidance.</div> Employee & Labor Relations https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49964 2026-01-06T16:45:46-07:00 2026-01-06T16:45:47-07:00 Instructor of Film Studies Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The School of Film &amp; Photography seeks qualified individuals to provide non-tenurable instruction in the following areas in the School’s Film Option: film and related media studies, film history.</div> School of Film and Photography https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/51101 2026-04-13T09:10:21-06:00 2026-04-13T09:10:21-06:00 MSSE Instructor Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The MSSE Instructor position is a non-tenure track instructor position for the Master of Science in Science Education (MSSE) degree program. It is an instructor position for a fall, spring, or summer graduate level science or education course. MSSE graduate students enrolled in the course are practicing K-12 teachers of science working in public and/or private institutions and non-traditional/informal instructional settings.</div> MSSE MS Science Education https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52720 2026-08-26T11:50:16-06:00 2026-08-26T11:50:17-06:00 Campus Planner <div>Under the general direction of the Director of PDC and the Planning Manager, this position performs a wide range of planning duties related to long range facilities planning programs for all Montana State University campuses and Montana Ag Experiment Stations (MAES). Primary responsibility of this position is to assist with and administer long range planning efforts and programs designed to meet and support the facilities growth plans, including the Strategic Plan, Long Range Master Planning, Long Range Building Program (LRBP), Capital Planning, Facilities Condition Inventory, space planning, transportation planning, wayfinding, and historic preservation. The position requires knowledge and skills managing resources, proficiency in written and oral communication and consensus building. The position duties include developing narratives and cost analysis of projects, programming efforts, inventorying space assets, and condition assessments, to assist the larger planning team, Director, and Associate Vice President. Related responsibilities include the management of data such as comprehensive Capital Projects database for major maintenance, additions, renovation, and historic preservation projects, and new construction projects.</div> Campus Planning, Design & Construction https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50070 2026-01-09T10:23:08-07:00 2026-01-09T10:23:08-07:00 Hospitality Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The Jake Jabs College of Business and Entrepreneurship offers a Bachelor of Science in Hospitality Management. To accomplish our mission, our teaching faculty should have professional experience in hospitality management. We seek experienced professionals with the ability to teach in more than one hospitality management area, including hotel management and operations and restaurant management and operations.</div> Jabs College of Business Instruct https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52624 2026-08-19T09:27:26-06:00 2026-08-19T09:27:27-06:00 Instructional Technology Specialist <div>The Instructional Technology Specialist serves as a campus expert and strategic partner in the effective use of MSU’s learning management system and related instructional technologies. This position combines LMS administration, technical problem-solving, faculty consultation, instructional technology support, and training to help faculty, staff, and students create effective, accessible learning experiences.</div> Center for Faculty Excellence https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49997 2026-01-07T09:57:05-07:00 2026-04-01T08:28:03-06:00 Culinary Arts Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty for the Culinary Arts program.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52079 2026-07-01T08:37:46-06:00 2026-07-01T08:37:46-06:00 Assistant to the Director <div>This position will support AHEC/MORH in conducting activities to align with the mission of the department by providing high-level administrative support to the Director while overseeing daily office operations to ensure an organized, efficient, and professional work environment. This role manages executive scheduling, travel, expense reconciliation, HR liaison responsibilities, recruitment coordination, event planning, and comprehensive administrative support to advance departmental effectiveness and compliance with University policies.</div> Montana AHEC/Rural Health https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52783 2026-09-01T16:23:17-06:00 2026-09-01T16:23:18-06:00 Equipment Operator II <div>The individual in this position will be a key player on the MSU Grounds/Waste team. Primarily focusing on waste, recycling and snow removal, this team player will complete a wide variety of duties in a great work environment.</div> Facility Services https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52735 2026-08-27T14:34:20-06:00 2026-08-27T14:34:21-06:00 Senior Project Manager <div>The Senior Project Manager (Senior PM) is a team leader responsible for managing Project Managers and Project Coordinators in support of project delivery on campus projects while also managing assigned projects directly as a project manager. The Senior PM collaborates with other managers within University Facilities Management to coordinate and prioritize the planning, design, and execution of projects within scope, schedule, and budget. The Senior PM keeps diverse and complex projects moving forward and helps advise the University on strategies to manage risks and improve processes.</div> Campus Planning, Design & Construction https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50033 2026-01-07T16:32:22-07:00 2026-01-07T16:32:23-07:00 American Studies Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The American Studies Program seeks instructors to teach American Studies courses on an as needed basis. The courses may be on-campus or online.</div> American Studies https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52440 2026-07-31T08:32:07-06:00 2026-07-31T08:32:07-06:00 Faculty Instructor & Bracken Business Center Coach for the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The Jake Jabs College of Business and Entrepreneurship at Montana State University seeks dynamic individuals who can blend the roles of faculty instructor and professional coach. As part of our commitment to offering a comprehensive business education, this unique position combines teaching responsibilities with coaching students in communication and career skills enhancement within the Bracken Center.<br><br>Candidates will contribute to our Bachelor of Science in Business program, offering options in Accounting, Finance, Management, Hospitality Business, and Marketing. A significant emphasis will be placed on incorporating real-world applications of theory into the curriculum, drawing on professional experience to mentor students in their professional development.<br><br>Ideal candidates will possess expertise in areas such as Accounting, Finance, Marketing, Management, Tax, Business Strategy, Digital Marketing, Entrepreneurship, Production Operations, and Law. Through one-on-one coaching sessions, small group appointments, workshops, and classroom instruction, faculty instructors will play a vital role in improving students' communication skills and professionalism within the Bracken Center. Join us in shaping the next generation of business leaders at Montana State University.</div> Jabs Program Fee https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52849 2026-09-04T16:32:40-06:00 2026-09-04T16:32:41-06:00 Director, Writing Center <div>The College of Letters &amp; Science is searching for a highly motivated and experienced educator to provide dynamic leadership for the Writing Center.</div> Writing Center https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49973 2026-01-06T17:36:40-07:00 2026-01-06T17:36:40-07:00 Accounting Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The Jake Jabs College of Business and Entrepreneurship offers a Bachelor of Science in Business, with a concentration in accounting degree. To accomplish our mission, a significant portion of our teaching faculty should have professional experience in practicing accounting. We seek experienced accounting professionals with the ability to teach in one or more accounting areas, including tax, data analytics, cost/managerial accounting, governmental/nonprofit accounting, financial accounting, fraud examination, and auditing.</div> Jabs College of Business Instruct https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/51221 2026-04-22T11:01:52-06:00 2026-04-22T11:01:52-06:00 Leadership Fellows Non-Tenure Track Faculty <div>The Leadership Fellows Certificate Program seeks instructors with experience and / or capacities in the following areas: experiential instruction, lived leadership experience, leadership theory, innovative and best practices in teaching in a seminar, small classroom format (&lt;20 students), leadership coaching, personal development, and working with learners in the young adult age group.</div> Leadership Fellows https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50072 2026-01-09T10:24:21-07:00 2026-01-09T10:24:22-07:00 Management & Entrepreneurship Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>TBD</div> Jabs College of Business Instruct https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52630 2026-08-19T14:03:09-06:00 2026-08-19T14:03:10-06:00 Cook I (Applicant Pool) <div>MSU’s Culinary Services hires motivated team members who are excited to actively participate in the ever changing world of the high-paced food industry.</div> Culinary Services Administration https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49999 2026-01-07T09:57:21-07:00 2026-01-07T09:57:21-07:00 Allied Health Phlebotomy Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty for the Phlebotomy program</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52104 2026-07-02T08:11:28-06:00 2026-07-02T08:11:29-06:00 HDCH Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The <a href=\"https://www.montana.edu/hdch/ \"><strong>Department of Human Development and Community Health</strong></a> seeks course instructors in the following areas:<br><br></div><ul><li>Community Health</li><li>Family and Consumer Sciences</li><li>Human Development and Family Science</li><li>Early Childhood Education (Preschool – Age 3)</li><li>Variable content courses</li></ul> Human Development &Community Health https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52789 2026-09-02T16:33:03-06:00 2026-09-02T16:33:04-06:00 Career Development Coordinator <div>The Career Development Coordinator oversees all activities related to career development within the LIFE Scholars program and works as an active member of the team to contribute to the overall mission of preparing graduates for meaningful, competitive, integrated employment.<br><br></div> Dean Educ/HHD https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/51437 2026-05-08T16:06:31-06:00 2026-05-08T16:06:31-06:00 Director of Enterprise Application Support <div>Establish tactical priorities, goals and initiatives. Develop, implement and support IT Knowledge Management best practices. Cultivate and maintain positive relationships with the University IT and 4-campus communities. Positively communicate, encourage, and assess technology needs and recommend best practices. Lead by example, projecting a positive attitude and a willingness to mentor and support others as needed.</div> UIT Business Operations https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52740 2026-08-27T16:37:16-06:00 2026-08-27T16:37:17-06:00 Police Officer Commissioned (POST Certified) <div>Recruiting highly motivated certified peace officers.<br><br><strong>This position is for certified applicants only.</strong></div> University Police https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50035 2026-01-07T16:40:30-07:00 2026-01-07T16:40:31-07:00 Physics Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The Department of Physics seeks a non-tenure track Assistant Teaching Professor or Instructor to teach various introductory and upper division physics and astronomy courses.</div> Physics https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52467 2026-08-04T08:44:11-06:00 2026-08-04T08:44:12-06:00 University Studies Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The University Studies program seeks instructors to teach the following class depending on need and available funding:<br>US101US First-Year Seminar</div> University Studies https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49980 2026-01-07T09:51:01-07:00 2026-01-07T09:51:02-07:00 Animal and Range Sciences Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) Animal & Range Sciences https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50145 2026-01-15T16:32:16-07:00 2026-01-15T16:32:17-07:00 Law Enforcement Academy, Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College is seeking a non-tenure track instructor to teach at the Law Enforcement Academy as a Lead Instructor or co-instructor. All curriculum has been developed and will be given to instructors at time of hire.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52676 2026-08-24T12:55:37-06:00 2026-08-24T12:55:38-06:00 Front Desk Services Coordinator <div>Join the University Student Housing team in providing support in one of our on-campus communities. Work as part of a student development team that provides support and services to on-campus students.</div> Residence Life Administration https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50002 2026-01-07T10:25:24-07:00 2026-01-07T10:25:25-07:00 Agricultural Economics & Economics Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) Agricultural Economics & Economics https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52182 2026-07-09T15:27:47-06:00 2026-07-09T15:27:48-06:00 Equine NTT Instructor/Assistant Foreman <div>The Equine Instructor/Assistant Foreman will oversee MSU's equine resources, facilities, and finances and will train students in Introductory and Intermediate Horsemanship (EQUH 114 Horsemanship I, EQUH 2IO Horsemanship II, and EQUH 310 Horsemanship IU), Colt Starting (EQUH 253 and 256). and develop a competitive Collegiate Ranch &amp; Stock Horse Team. The position will work closely with Equine Science faculty and livestock operations staff to maintain a safe, effective, and high-quality learning environment for students and horses.</div> Animal & Range Sciences https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52801 2026-09-03T13:56:42-06:00 2026-09-03T13:56:43-06:00 Agronomic Entomologist <div>Montana State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Agronomic Entomology in the Department of Plant Sciences and Plant Pathology. The successful candidate will develop an innovative, externally funded research program addressing fundamental and applied questions in the biology, ecology, and management of insects in agricultural systems. The position offers opportunities to collaborate across a diverse community of agricultural and biological scientists and to engage with Montana’s agricultural stakeholders. Teaching will contribute to our growing entomology programs, including courses such as Integrated Pest Management and Insect Physiology.</div> Plant Sciences https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/51514 2026-05-15T09:57:00-06:00 2026-05-15T09:57:00-06:00 Plant Sciences & Plant Pathology Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) Plant Sciences https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52747 2026-08-28T16:43:17-06:00 2026-08-28T16:43:18-06:00 Assistant Professor of Mechanical Engineering <div>The Mechanical &amp; Industrial Engineering (M&amp;IE) Department at Montana State University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor. The primary responsibilities include teaching both undergraduate and graduate courses focused in mechanical engineering, developing a sustained, commendable, distinguished, and externally-funded research program, and participating in professional/service activities.</div> Mechanical & Industrial Engineering https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50037 2026-01-07T16:46:20-07:00 2026-01-07T16:46:20-07:00 Arabic Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>Department of Modern Languages and Literatures maintains an applicant pool for Non-Tenure Track Instructors in Arabic. Instructors typically teach 1 to 5 language classes per semester. All positions are pending adequate enrollment and funding. This advertisement is for an applicant pool. It does not indicate whether or not there are any current openings. Qualified candidates will be contacted in the event a position opens.</div> Modern Languages & Literature https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52498 2026-08-05T15:05:18-06:00 2026-08-05T15:05:20-06:00 Extension Grant and Fiscal Coordinator <div>The Extension Grant and Fiscal coordinator plays a vital role in supporting research and funding efforts within Montana State University Extension. This position collaborates with principal investigators, administrative staff, and funding agencies to facilitate grant proposal development, submission, and compliance. In collaboration with MSU’s Office of Sponsored Programs and Office of Research Development, this position will support and advise Extension faculty and staff in identifying, developing, submitting, and managing grants and contracts; managing resource expenditures including invoicing and reporting; preparing a variety of fiscal reports; utilizing CatBooks, Banner, Chrome River, and other accounting software; and working as a member of the MSU Extension Finance Team to assist with other duties.</div> Administration - MSU Extension https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49983 2026-01-07T09:54:28-07:00 2026-01-07T09:54:29-07:00 Photonics & Laser Technology Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty for the Photonics &amp; Laser Technology program.<br><br><br></div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52815 2026-09-03T16:18:47-06:00 2026-09-03T16:18:48-06:00 Livestock and Farm Assistant Manager <div>The employee will interact with research professionals, faculty, the Superintendent, and the Department Head in general support of the commodity production, research, and educational programs of the research center and the department.</div> AES NARC https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/42083 2024-06-19T18:22:32-06:00 2024-06-19T18:22:32-06:00 Postdoctoral Fellowship - Development of Innovative Airborne Communication Systems <div>The Spectrum Lab (https://spectrum.montana.edu/index.html) and the Geospatial Snow, Water, and Ice Resources Lab (GeoSWIRL; https://arcg.is/0ObXba) at Montana State University are recruiting a Postdoctoral Fellow. The postdoc will focus on developing and deploying novel communications systems that leverage advanced computing, tethered balloons, and UAVs (Uncrewed Aerial Vehicles).</div> Earth Sciences https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50441 2026-02-20T15:12:33-07:00 2026-02-20T15:12:33-07:00 Analytics Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The Jake Jabs College of Business and Entrepreneurship offers a Bachelor of Science in Business, with required and elective analytics courses throughout the curriculum for all concentrations (management, marketing, finance, accounting, and hospitality management). Analytics courses are also taught in the M.S. in Innovation and Management graduate program. Primarily, we are seeking experienced analytics professionals capable of teaching a variety of established analytics courses within our curriculum, which includes business analytics, data analytics I and II, operations management, applied data science, and operations and supply chain management. Additionally, we are interested in candidates capable of developing analytics coursework in contemporary and industry-relevant areas in our concentrations.</div> Jabs College of Business Instruct https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52688 2026-08-25T08:39:14-06:00 2026-08-25T08:39:15-06:00 Research Scientist <div>The Center for Health and Safety Culture is seeking a Research Scientist to<strong> </strong>contribute to Center research, technology transfer and support services by making contributions to the definition, measurement, and transformation of culture, evaluation services, training, and/or training resources.<br><br></div><div>We are a highly collaborative team of researchers and scientists from diverse fields who, together, share in their passion for improving health and safety and strengthening communities. Every day we come to work eager to solve complex problems and make the world a better place.<br><br></div><div>This position will support the team across multiple projects addressing health and safety. This position offers an exciting opportunity for an individual with a passion for growing safe and healthy behaviors within communities.</div> Center for Health & Safety Culture https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50005 2026-01-07T12:01:23-07:00 2026-01-07T12:01:24-07:00 Gianforte School of Computing Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The Gianforte School of Computing seeks instructors for courses that are taught on a regular basis. Please refer to <a href=\"http://www.cs.montana.edu/courses.html\"><strong>http://www.cs.montana.edu/courses.html</strong></a> for an overview of our courses.</div> Gianforte School of Computing https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52244 2026-07-15T14:27:20-06:00 2026-07-15T14:27:20-06:00 Assistant Professor – Instruction and Open Strategies Librarian <div>This tenure-track librarian will focus on library open strategies and offer library instruction, including providing strategic direction across the library with open technologies, open research, open education and pedagogy, and scholarly communication; being a member of the library instruction department, offering credited and embedded instruction to students, staff, and faculty; and contributing scholarship and service.</div> Library https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49985 2026-01-07T09:54:38-07:00 2026-01-07T09:54:38-07:00 Interior Design Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty for the Interior Design program.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/51680 2026-06-01T12:33:51-06:00 2026-06-01T12:33:51-06:00 Cashier Full-Time (Applicant Pool) <div>MSU’s Culinary Services hires motivated team members who are excited to actively participate in the ever changing world of the high-paced food industry.</div> Culinary Services Administration https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52753 2026-08-31T09:25:39-06:00 2026-08-31T09:25:40-06:00 Subaward Manager <div>The <strong>Subaward Manager&nbsp;</strong>represents a great opportunity in the Office of Sponsored Programs (OSP) for a dynamic candidate with exceptional multi-tasking and organizational skills. The individual in this position will provide direct financial and administrative support to the OSP Subaward area.</div> Office of Sponsored Programs Admin https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50039 2026-01-07T16:50:07-07:00 2026-01-07T16:50:07-07:00 German Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>Department of Modern Languages and Literatures maintains an applicant pool for Non-Tenure Track Instructors in German. Instructors typically teach 1 to 5 language classes per semester. All positions are pending adequate enrollment and funding. This advertisement is for an applicant pool. It does not indicate whether or not there are any current openings. Qualified candidates will be contacted in the event a position comes open.</div> Modern Languages & Literature https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52523 2026-08-07T09:46:14-06:00 2026-08-07T09:46:15-06:00 Academic Advisor II <div>The College of Letters and Science is looking for a collegial, dynamic, and motivated individual who is dedicated to student success and is able to thrive in an environment that includes frequent interactions with students, faculty, and staff. The Academic Advisor II provides critical support to the Master of Science in Science Education (MSSE) program.</div> MSSE MS Science Education https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52273 2026-07-16T16:48:35-06:00 2026-07-16T16:48:35-06:00 Sociology & Anthropology Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The Department of Sociology and Anthropology seeks a non-tenure track assistant teaching professor or instructor to teach an array of upper and lower division courses during the academic year. The new faculty member will be expected to contribute to excellence in undergraduate teaching in the areas of sociology, and/or criminology, or anthropology related to the applicant’s strength.</div> Sociology & Anthropology https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52821 2026-09-03T16:36:09-06:00 2026-09-03T16:36:10-06:00 Lab Manager <div>The Evans Lab in the Department of Microbiology and Cell Biology is seeking a highly skilled and motivated Research Lab Manager to conduct research activities and oversee lab functions.</div> Microbiology & Cell Biology https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49936 2026-01-06T11:38:07-07:00 2026-01-06T11:38:08-07:00 Counseling Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The <a href=\"https://www.montana.edu/counselingdepartment/\"><strong>Department of Counseling</strong></a> seeks course instructors based on need and availability in the following areas:<br><br></div><ul><li>Practicum</li><li>Internship</li><li>Variable content courses</li></ul> Counseling https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50724 2026-03-13T09:53:44-06:00 2026-03-13T09:53:45-06:00 Gen Ed - Social Sciences Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty to teach Social Science courses in the AA/AS program.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52694 2026-08-25T10:11:13-06:00 2026-08-25T10:11:14-06:00 Administrative Associate IV <div>We are seeking a highly organized, detail-oriented, and customer-focused Administrative Associate IV to support the financial and administrative operations of the Montana Seed Potato Certification Program, Montana Potato Improvement Association (MPIA), and the MSU Potato Laboratory. This position serves as the primary administrative and financial support for the program by coordinating accounting and bookkeeping activities, grower billing, financial reporting, grant monitoring, payroll tracking, meeting and travel coordination, records management, and personnel support. The successful candidate will work closely with the Director, Administrative/Program Manager, growers, board members, Extension personnel, and Fiscal Shared Services to ensure efficient daily operations while maintaining accurate financial records and providing outstanding customer service.</div> Plant Sciences https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50007 2026-01-07T12:11:01-07:00 2026-01-07T12:11:02-07:00 College of Engineering Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The College of Engineering’s (COE) Multidisciplinary Engineering Design course is taught by faculty who bring real-world experience into the classroom. These faculty members are expected to instruct and mentor student project teams through their first open-ended, multidisciplinary design experience. Other responsibilities include advising and mentoring undergraduate students, participation in accreditation activities and committee assignments, and service to the University, State, and profession.</div> Eng Dean's Support https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49987 2026-01-07T09:54:48-07:00 2026-01-07T09:54:49-07:00 Developmental Math Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty for Developmental Math.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/51817 2026-06-10T12:45:20-06:00 2026-06-10T12:45:21-06:00 Mathematics, Mathematics Education and Statistics Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The MSU Mathematical Sciences Department maintains a pool of Non-Tenure-Track applicants for consideration as potential instructors in mathematics, mathematics education and statistics courses.</div> Mathematical Sciences https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52758 2026-08-31T11:12:29-06:00 2026-08-31T11:12:30-06:00 CARC Administrative Associate III <div>The Administrative Associate III performs a variety of administrative support, personnel &amp; payroll, and accounting duties for the Central Agricultural Research Center (CARC), located at Moccasin, MT. This includes providing administrative assistance to the superintendent and direct support for faculty and staff at the center. The Administrative Associate III represents CARC and its interests to entities outside and within the university and plays an active role in the planning and administering day-to-day operations of the front office. The person in this position reconciles funds and monitors account balance, generates payment authorizations and reports, and assists in arranging center meetings and large-scale functions.</div> AES CARC https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50041 2026-01-07T16:54:04-07:00 2026-01-07T16:54:04-07:00 Spanish Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>Department of Modern Languages and Literatures maintains an applicant pool for Non-Tenure Track Instructors in Spanish. Instructors typically teach 1 to 5 language classes per semester. All positions are pending adequate enrollment and funding. This advertisement is for an applicant pool. It does not indicate whether or not there are any current openings. Qualified candidates will be contacted in the event a position opens.</div> Modern Languages & Literature https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52538 2026-08-10T12:14:50-06:00 2026-08-10T12:14:51-06:00 Graphic Designer <div>The Graphic Designer oversees the planning, design, and production of marketing and communications materials across print, digital, social media, video, and advertising platforms for Museum of the Rockies. This position manages creative project workflows, maintains brand standards, and produces high-quality visual communications that support organizational goals.</div> Museum of the Rockies https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52315 2026-07-21T09:46:32-06:00 2026-07-21T09:46:33-06:00 Education Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The <a href=\"https://www.montana.edu/education/ \"><strong>Department of Education</strong></a> seeks course instructors in the following specialty areas:<br><br></div><ul><li>Teacher Education – Generalist (Curriculum Design, Assessment)</li><li>Teacher Education – Science Methods</li><li>Teacher Education – Social Studies Methods</li><li>Teacher Education – English Language Arts</li><li>Mathematics Education</li><li>Educational Technology</li><li>Educational Leadership</li><li>Adult Education</li><li>Higher Education</li><li>Curriculum &amp; Instruction</li><li>Library Media Certificate</li></ul> Education https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52828 2026-09-03T16:51:34-06:00 2026-09-03T16:51:34-06:00 Research Associate - Field Research Program <div>This position will work under the supervision of the Associate Professor of Plant Pathology at the Eastern Agricultural Research Center to manage and conduct field research projects focused on crop disease management and agricultural production systems. Responsibilities include establishing and maintaining research plots, collecting field data, managing research activities, performing data analysis, preparing reports and manuscripts, and supervising seasonal employees and student workers.<br><br></div><div>This position provides an excellent opportunity for an early-career scientist to develop advanced skills in applied agricultural research, including field experiment management, research data collection and analysis, scientific communication, and supervision of research personnel. The successful candidate will gain experience working across a diverse portfolio of grant-funded research projects while contributing to research outcomes that support agricultural production in the Northern Great Plains.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate will be an experienced field researcher who enjoys hands-on agricultural research, working outdoors, and being part of a small collaborative research team within a rural agricultural community. This position requires flexibility, attention to detail, problem-solving skills, and a willingness to work together with other team members to successfully complete research objectives.</div> AES EARC https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49942 2026-01-06T13:29:59-07:00 2026-01-06T13:29:59-07:00 Instructor of Photography Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The School of Film &amp; Photography seeks qualified individuals to provide<br>non-tenurable instruction in the following areas: <strong>photography (analog and digital), photo history, and new media</strong>.</div> School of Film and Photography https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50726 2026-03-13T09:55:57-06:00 2026-03-13T09:55:57-06:00 Gen Ed - Humanities Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty for Humanities courses within the AA/AS program.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52709 2026-08-25T14:29:29-06:00 2026-08-25T14:29:30-06:00 EARC Administrative Associate III <div>The Eastern Agricultural Research Center (EARC) located in Sidney, MT is looking for a dependable, organized, and personable administrative professional to support the work of the research center.<br><br></div><div>The Administrative Associate III serves as the primary contact for the center's front office and works closely with the Superintendent, faculty, researchers, and staff on day-to-day administrative, financial, purchasing, personnel, and event-related activities.<br><br>The Administrative Associate III represents EARC and its interests to entities outside and within the university.</div> AES EARC https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50011 2026-01-07T12:26:36-07:00 2026-01-07T12:26:36-07:00 Psychology Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>Montana State University seeks qualified individuals to provide non-tenurable level instruction and/or related functions. Applications are accepted on a continual basis (unless otherwise indicated) and will be maintained in the pool for two years. After two years, candidates need to re-submit materials for continued consideration.</div> Psychology https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49989 2026-01-07T09:54:58-07:00 2026-01-07T09:54:59-07:00 Welding Technology Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty for the Welding Technology program</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/51876 2026-06-15T13:56:07-06:00 2026-06-15T13:56:08-06:00 Catering Floor Supervisor <div>MSU Catering is looking for motivated team members who are excited to actively participate in the ever changing world of the high-paced food and catering industries.</div> University Catering https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52771 2026-09-01T09:28:00-06:00 2026-09-01T09:28:01-06:00 Extension Agent - Granite County <div>This position is located in <strong>Philipsburg, Montana.</strong></div><div><br></div><div>The primary duty for County Extension Faculty is to assess local community needs, then to develop, implement, and evaluate Extension programming to meet those needs. The primary emphasis of the Granite County Extension Agent position is in the areas of Agriculture, Natural Resources and 4-H Youth Development<em> </em>with secondary emphasis on Community Vitality and Family and Consumer Sciences<em>. </em>The Granite County Extension office is staffed by a full-time administrative assistant.</div> Extension Agents/Field https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50043 2026-01-07T17:01:11-07:00 2026-01-07T17:01:11-07:00 Honors College HONR 201 and 202 Texts and Critics Instructor (Applicant Pool) <div>The Honors College seeks individuals to serve as instructors for HONR 201 and 202, Texts and Critics, the interdisciplinary seminar for first-year honors college students.</div><ul><li>We are especially interested in candidates who, through their life experiences, research, teaching, and/or service, will contribute to excellence in undergraduate education in the Honors College at Montana State University.</li><li>We require candidates who are excited about a classroom environment where student voices are centered.</li><li>We welcome applications from individuals who may have had nontraditional career paths, or who have excelled in careers outside of academia.</li><li>We seek candidates who possess effective interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills and have the ability to contribute to the academic success and retention of honors college students.</li></ul> Honors College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52590 2026-08-14T10:01:38-06:00 2026-08-14T10:01:39-06:00 Career Education Coach <div>Support students in developing career readiness through coaching, workshops, and classroom engagement. This part-time role is ideal for professionals passionate about mentoring students and facilitating career development.</div> Career Services https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50014 2026-01-07T12:41:14-07:00 2026-01-07T12:41:15-07:00 Chemistry and Biochemistry Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry seeks a non-tenure track Instructor to teach in the areas of general chemistry, organic chemistry, analytical chemistry, and biochemistry.</div> Chemistry https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52318 2026-07-21T10:25:33-06:00 2026-07-21T10:25:33-06:00 Instructor of Architecture Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The School of Architecture seeks an instructor(s) qualified to teach one or more of the following courses in Environmental Design/Architecture depending upon available funding:<strong>Funding, Architectural Design Studios, Architectural Structures, Architectural Graphics, Graduate Level Elective Courses, Professional Practice, Building Construction, Sustainability, Research Methods, Theory, Environmental Control Systems.</strong></div> Architecture https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52835 2026-09-04T09:51:43-06:00 2026-09-04T09:51:44-06:00 Custodian I - Part-Time - Pool <div>Residence Life Custodians provide cleaning and light maintenance services for the residence halls and associated areas. This part-time position is for up to 16hours per week.</div> Residence Life Administration https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49952 2026-01-06T15:27:13-07:00 2026-01-06T15:27:14-07:00 Instructor of Art Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The School of Art seeks qualified individuals to provide non-tenurable instruction in the following areas:<br><br></div><ul><li>VISUAL LANGUAGE 2D</li><li>VISUAL LANGUAGE 3D</li><li>LANGUAGE DRAWING</li><li>CERAMICS, SCULPTURE</li><li>PAINTING, METALSMITHING</li><li>GRAPHIC DESIGN</li><li>ART HISTORY</li></ul> Art https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50953 2026-03-31T13:48:03-06:00 2026-04-28T08:42:46-06:00 University Studies and College Success Non-Tenure Track Faculty <div>University Studies seeks qualified individuals to teach introductory student success-oriented courses, each of which focus on a unique topic, such as Learning Strategies, Career Exploration, adventure learning, service-learning, and Intro to Health Professions.</div> University Studies https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52713 2026-08-25T16:03:30-06:00 2026-08-25T16:03:32-06:00 Fire Marshal <div>Responsible for ﬁre code application and enforcement, ﬁre code inspections, ﬁre systems inspections/testing, code review for new construction and major renovations, fire drills and associated coordination, fire extinguisher program, and ﬁre and life safety-related training.</div> Safety & Risk Mgmt https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52601 2026-08-14T15:54:20-06:00 2026-08-14T15:54:21-06:00 Finance Director <div>The Finance Director in the Technology Transfer Office (TTO) serves as the primary financial professional for the department. In collaboration with TTO leadership, this position ensures departmental financial integrity, effective resource management, efficient processes, and alignment with organizational goals. The role manages complex activities unique to technology transfer and is a rare opportunity to apply financial leadership skills in an innovative environment that supports university research commercialization, technology licensing, entrepreneurship and startup development.</div> MSU Technology Transfer Office https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49994 2026-01-07T09:55:22-07:00 2026-04-01T08:28:03-06:00 Culinary Arts Chef Manager Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seeks a part-time chef manager for the Culinary Arts program.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52009 2026-06-25T16:58:38-06:00 2026-06-25T16:58:38-06:00 Assistant Professor of Microbiology <div>Assistant Professor of Microbiology</div> Microbiology & Cell Biology https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52776 2026-09-01T11:14:45-06:00 2026-09-01T11:14:47-06:00 Director of University News and Media Relations <div>The Director of University News and Media Relations leads the MSU News Service and oversees Montana State University’s central news, media relations and public information functions. The position advances MSU’s reputation through accurate, timely and compelling storytelling; productive relationships with journalists; thoughtful public information planning; and coordinated communication during campus incidents and emergencies. The director also provides editorial leadership, media strategy, issue monitoring, media training and communications advice across the university.</div> University Communications https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50047 2026-01-07T17:14:04-07:00 2026-01-07T17:14:04-07:00 Microbiology & Cell Biology Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) Microbiology & Cell Biology https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50029 2026-01-07T15:51:06-07:00 2026-01-07T15:51:07-07:00 Creative Writing Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The MSU English Department maintains a pool of non-tenure-track applicants for consideration as potential instructors in creative writing courses.</div> English https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52409 2026-07-28T14:05:56-06:00 2026-07-28T14:05:57-06:00 Grants and Fiscal Manager <div>The Grants and Fiscal Manager will coordinate and manage the fiscal and human resources activities of the Western Transportation Institute (WTI), including assisting in the fiscal oversight of the Local Technical Assistance Program (LTAP) and the National Center for Rural Road Safety. The Grants and Fiscal Manager will monitor grant and contract funding (including necessary matching funds), develop and implement policies and procedures to ensure maximum efficiency, productivity, and accountability of the administrative and overall functions of WTI.</div> Western Transportation Institute https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52838 2026-09-04T12:57:08-06:00 2026-09-04T12:57:09-06:00 University Human Resources Analyst <div>The University Human Resources (UHR) Data Analyst works closely with the Compliance Specialist, Service Center Director, and Payroll Director to ensure the accuracy, integrity, and efficiency of UHR Data. This position performs advanced data analysis, reporting, system maintenance, troubleshooting, and testing to support University Human Resources operations and strategic initiatives.<br><br></div><div>The Analyst collaborates with University Information Technology (UIT), University Data Analytics (UDA), and other campus departments to optimize UHR systems, improve business processes, maintain data integrity throughout the employee lifecycle, and support informed decision-making through accurate reporting and process automation. This position is in person in Bozeman, MT not eligible for remote work.<br><br><strong>This is an on-site position located in Bozeman, MT and is not eligible for remote work.</strong></div> HR Comp Ben Empl Services https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49962 2026-01-06T16:33:08-07:00 2026-01-06T16:33:08-07:00 Food Systems, Nutrition, and Kinesiology Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The <a href=\"https://www.montana.edu/fsnk/\"><strong>Department of Food Systems, Nutrition, and Kinesiology</strong></a> seeks course instructors in the following areas:<br><br></div><ul><li>Food and Nutrition</li><li>Sustainable Food Systems</li><li>Hospitality Management</li><li>Kinesiology</li><li>Health Enhancement (Physical and Health Education)</li><li>Coaching</li></ul> Food Systems Nutrition & Kinesiolog https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50979 2026-04-01T10:42:22-06:00 2026-04-01T10:42:22-06:00 History Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The MSU History &amp; Philosophy Department maintains a pool of non-tenure-track applicants for consideration as potential instructors.</div> History and Philosophy https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52719 2026-08-26T11:30:56-06:00 2026-08-26T11:30:57-06:00 Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Nursing <div>The Mark and Robyn Jones College of Nursing is searching for Assistant/Associate/Full tenure-track faculty with primary responsibilities teaching both undergraduate and graduate courses in nursing, developing and/or sustaining a funded program of research, and participating in professional/service activities.</div> Nursing Departments https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50050 2026-01-08T09:03:05-07:00 2026-01-08T09:03:05-07:00 Land Resources & Environmental Sciences Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) Land Resources & Environ Sci https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52614 2026-08-18T08:47:19-06:00 2026-08-18T08:47:21-06:00 Information Technology User Services IT Asset & Hardware Logistics Specialist <div>This position supports University Information Technology (UIT) by managing the receiving, tagging, inventory tracking, and campus delivery of IT hardware. It ensures accurate asset records, timely distribution, and coordination with vendors and campus partners for hardware orders and deliveries.</div> UIT USG  Desktop Support https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49996 2026-01-07T09:56:48-07:00 2026-01-07T09:56:49-07:00 Aviation Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52077 2026-07-01T08:28:40-06:00 2026-07-01T08:28:40-06:00 Flathead County Agriculture Extension Agent <div><strong>This position resides at the MSU Flathead County Extension Office in Kalispell, Montana<br></strong><br></div><div>The primary duty for County Extension Faculty is to assess local community needs, then develop, implement, and evaluate Extension programming to meet those needs. The main emphasis of the Flathead County Agriculture Agent position will be in the areas of horticulture, agriculture, and natural resources.<br><br></div><div>As a member of the faculty team leading MSU Extension education for the people of Flathead County, efforts will address current and emerging locally identified opportunities for Flathead County. Foci of this position are to improve the long-term success of horticulture practitioners, agricultural enterprises, natural resource managers, and 4-H Youth Development. It is anticipated that the intensity of focus within identified disciplines will be adjusted to address local trends. Flathead County faculty actively pursue multi-disciplinary programming, and the successful candidate will work with 4-H Youth Development faculty as appropriate, to plan, implement and evaluate multi-disciplinary programs.<br><br></div><div>The MSU Extension Flathead County Office also has an agent for 4-H Youth Development, an agent for Family and Consumers Sciences and 4-H Youth Development, and a full-time administrative professional.</div> Extension Agents/Field https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52781 2026-09-01T16:09:18-06:00 2026-09-01T16:09:19-06:00 Postdoctoral Researcher - Lyme Disease Bacteriophage Biology <div>The Secor Lab seeks a postdoctoral researcher to investigate bacteriophage biology in the Lyme disease spirochete Borrelia burgdorferi. The successful candidate will help define how phiBB-1 controls horizontal gene transfer and bacterial adaptation across the tick-mouse infectious cycle.</div> Microbiology & Cell Biology https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/50031 2026-01-07T16:30:13-07:00 2026-01-07T16:30:13-07:00 Technical Writing Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div>The MSU English Department maintains a pool of non-tenure-track applicants for consideration as potential instructors in writing courses.</div> English https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52430 2026-07-29T15:44:43-06:00 2026-07-29T15:44:44-06:00 Gen Ed – Health Sciences Non-Tenure Track Faculty – Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) <div>Gallatin College seek a Health Sciences non-tenure track faculty for the AA/AS program.</div> Gallatin College https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52840 2026-09-04T13:27:20-06:00 2026-09-04T13:27:21-06:00 Director of Procurement & Contract Services <div>Montana State University is seeking a strategic and collaborative leader to serve as Director of Procurement and Contract Services. This role provides executive oversight of the university’s procurement function, contracts for goods and services, and guides the strategic use of the university procure-to-pay system (Jaggaer), collaborating across Financial Services to ensure an efficient and all-inclusive process.<br><br>Reporting to the Associate Vice President for Financial Services, the Director is responsible for setting strategy, ensuring compliance with state law, Board of Regents policy, and university procedures, and delivering a seamless, customer-focused experience for campus stakeholders.</div> Procurement Services https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/49966 2026-01-06T16:57:08-07:00 2026-01-06T16:57:08-07:00 Librarian/Instructor Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) <div><strong>This is a posting to gather a pool of qualified applicants for possible Librarian and other professional openings, on an as needed basis. </strong>Work may involve reference and instructional service, other functional specialties as needed, and/or special projects.</div> Library https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/51218 2026-04-22T09:39:00-06:00 2026-04-22T09:39:01-06:00 Agricultural Economics & Economics Non-Tenure Track Visiting Instructor (Applicant Pool) <div>The department seeks candidates for a Visiting Instructor position during the Academic Year 2026-27 to teach a 3-3 (0.6 FTE) load that includes courses in intermediate microeconomics, principles of macroeconomics, and intermediate macroeconomics.&nbsp;</div> Agricultural Economics & Economics https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52722 2026-08-26T14:04:43-06:00 2026-08-26T14:04:44-06:00 Extension Agent – Family and Consumer Sciences and 4-H Youth Development – Pondera County <div>This position is located in <strong>Conrad, Montana.<br></strong><br></div><div>The primary duty for County Extension Faculty is to assess local community needs, then to develop, implement, and evaluate Extension programming to meet those needs. The primary emphases of the Pondera County Extension Agent position are in the areas of Family and Consumer Sciences and 4-H Youth Development, with secondary emphasis on Community Vitality. The Pondera County Extension office is staffed by an Agriculture and 4-H Youth Development agent, a Family and Consumer Sciences and 4-H Youth Development agent, and one full-time administrative assistant.</div> Extension Agents/Field"
    },
