hires motivated team members who are excited to actively participate in the ever changing world of the high-paced food industry. View Details Bookmark Postdoctoral Researcher – Political Science and Systems Engineering STAFF - VA - 26364 College of Letters & Science Political Science Staff Join an interdisciplinary postdoctoral fellowship at Montana State University, in collaboration with engineering and political science faculty, to implement an existing research program defined in the DigiCARES strategic plan that advances justice-enhanced resilience in next-generation energy system digital twins. The position offers hands-on research using real-world utility data and community... View Details Bookmark Plant Sciences & Plant Pathology Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26080 College of Agriculture Plant Sciences Faculty View Details Bookmark NAGPRA Program Lead STAFF - VA - 26406 Office of Research and Economic Development Research Integrity and Compliance Staff The NAGPRA Program Leadcoordinates compliance, consultations, repatriations, and other activities associated with ensuring MSU’s compliance with the Native American Graves Protection and Repatriation Act (NAGPRA) federal regulation by coordinating inventory and curation of Native American artifacts and remains. This position will work to strengthen MSU’s NAGPRA program and will report directly ... View Details Bookmark Director of Enterprise Application Support STAFF - VA - 26399 VP for Information Technology UIT Business Operations Staff Establish tactical priorities, goals and initiatives. Develop, implement and support IT Knowledge Management best practices. Cultivate and maintain positive relationships with the University IT and 4-campus communities. Positively communicate, encourage, and assess technology needs and recommend best practices. Lead by example, projecting a positive attitude and a willingness to mentor and supp... View Details Bookmark Police Officer Commissioned (non-certified) STAFF - VA - 26215 Administration University Police Staff A Police Officer Commissioned (non-certified) is a police officer candidate who does not currently hold a Montana, or an out-of-state equivalent, POST certificate. The successful candidate will attend the Montana Law Enforcement Academy Law Enforcement Officer Basic Course in Helena, MT, for three months.Montana State University police officers provide a safe and secure environment for living a... View Details Bookmark Leadership Fellows Non-Tenure Track Faculty FAC - VA - 26133 Office of Academic Affairs Leadership Fellows Faculty The Leadership Fellows Certificate Program seeks instructors with experience and / or capacities in the following areas: experiential instruction, lived leadership experience, leadership theory, innovative and best practices in teaching in a seminar, small classroom format (<20 students), leadership coaching, personal development, and working with learners in the young adult age group. View Details Bookmark Agricultural Economics & Economics Non-Tenure Track Visiting Instructor (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26134 College of Agriculture Agricultural Economics & Economics Faculty The department seeks candidates for a Visiting Instructor position during the Academic Year 2026-27 to teach a 3-3 (0.6 FTE) load that includes courses in intermediate microeconomics, principles of macroeconomics, and intermediate macroeconomics. View Details Bookmark MSSE Instructor Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26112 College of Letters & Science MSSE MS Science Education Faculty The MSSE Instructor position is a non-tenure track instructor position for the Master of Science in Science Education (MSSE) degree program. It is an instructor position for a fall, spring, or summer graduate level science or education course. MSSE graduate students enrolled in the course are practicing K-12 teachers of science working in public and/or private institutions and non-traditional/i... View Details Bookmark History Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26093 College of Letters & Science History and Philosophy Faculty The MSU History & Philosophy Department maintains a pool of non-tenure-track applicants for consideration as potential instructors. View Details Bookmark Philosophy Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26094 College of Letters & Science History and Philosophy Faculty The Department of History and Philosophy seeks course instructors in the disciplines of philosophy on an as needed basis. View Details Bookmark University Studies and College Success Non-Tenure Track Faculty FAC - VA - 26130 Office of Academic Affairs University Studies Faculty University Studies seeks qualified individuals to teach introductory student success-oriented courses, each of which focus on a unique topic, such as Learning Strategies, Career Exploration, adventure learning, service-learning, and Intro to Health Professions. View Details Bookmark Earth Sciences Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26118 College of Letters & Science Earth Sciences Faculty The Department of Earth Sciences at Montana State University seeks Non-Tenure Track Faculty to teach various Earth Sciences courses to undergraduate and graduate students. View Details Bookmark Gen Ed - Humanities Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26038 Gallatin College Gallatin College Faculty Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty for Humanities courses within the AA/AS program. View Details Bookmark Gen Ed - Natural Sciences Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26055 Gallatin College Gallatin College Faculty Gallatin College seeks Natural Science non-tenure track faculty for the AA/AS program. View Details Bookmark Gen Ed - Social Sciences Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26058 Gallatin College Gallatin College Faculty Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty to teach Social Science courses in the AA/AS program. View Details Bookmark Gen Ed - Workforce Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26059 Gallatin College Gallatin College Faculty Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty for general education courses for the workforce programs. View Details Bookmark Analytics Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26123 College of Business Jabs College of Business Instruct Faculty The Jake Jabs College of Business and Entrepreneurship offers a Bachelor of Science in Business, with required and elective analytics courses throughout the curriculum for all concentrations (management, marketing, finance, accounting, and hospitality management). Analytics courses are also taught in the M.S. in Innovation and Management graduate program. Primarily, we are seeking experienced a... View Details Bookmark Mechanical & Industrial Engineering Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26088 College of Engineering Mechanical & Industrial Engineering Faculty Mechanical & Industrial Engineering faculty members are expected to contribute to excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching in areas of mechanical engineering, mechanical engineering technology or industrial engineering related to the applicant’s strengths. Other responsibilities include advising and mentoring undergraduate students, participation in accreditation activities and com... View Details Bookmark Law Enforcement Academy, Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26120 Gallatin College Gallatin College Faculty Gallatin College is seeking a non-tenure track instructor to teach at the Law Enforcement Academy as a Lead Instructor or co-instructor. All curriculum has been developed and will be given to instructors at time of hire. View Details Bookmark COMX 111US Public Speaking Instructor Non-Tenure Track (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26119 Office of Academic Affairs University Studies Faculty The University Studies Program seeks instructors to teach the following class depending on need and available funding: COMX 111US Introduction to Public Speaking View Details Bookmark Management & Entrepreneurship Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26073 College of Business Jabs College of Business Instruct Faculty TBD View Details Bookmark Finance Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26072 College of Business Jabs College of Business Instruct Faculty The Jake Jabs College of Business and Entrepreneurship offers a Bachelor of Science in Business, with a concentration in finance degree. To accomplish our mission, a significant portion of our teaching faculty should have professional experience in practicing financial management. We seek experienced finance professionals with the ability to teach in more than one area, including financial mark... View Details Bookmark Hospitality Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26074 College of Business Jabs College of Business Instruct Faculty The Jake Jabs College of Business and Entrepreneurship offers a Bachelor of Science in Hospitality Management. To accomplish our mission, our teaching faculty should have professional experience in hospitality management. We seek experienced professionals with the ability to teach in more than one hospitality management area, including hotel management and operations and restaurant management a... View Details Bookmark Land Resources & Environmental Sciences Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26113 College of Agriculture Land Resources & Environ Sci Faculty View Details Bookmark NTT Faculty Instructors for MCB/MMLS College of Ag (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26116 College of Agriculture Microbiology & Cell Biology Faculty View Details Bookmark Microbiology & Cell Biology Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26115 College of Agriculture Microbiology & Cell Biology Faculty View Details Bookmark Cooperative Veterinary Medicine Program Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26114 College of Agriculture Veterinary Medicine WIMU Faculty View Details Bookmark Honors College HONR 201 and 202 Texts and Critics Instructor (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26111 Honors College Honors College Faculty The Honors College seeks individuals to serve as instructors for HONR 201 and 202, Texts and Critics, the interdisciplinary seminar for first-year honors college students.We are especially interested in candidates who, through their life experiences, research, teaching, and/or service, will contribute to excellence in undergraduate education in the Honors College at Montana State University.We ... View Details Bookmark Liberal Studies Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26110 College of Letters & Science Liberal Studies Faculty Montana State University’s Liberal Studies program, located in the College of Letters & Science, provides undergraduate students with a broad, integrated, and interdisciplinary learning experience. The Liberal Studies program seeks pool applications for potential instructors typically for LS 101 and/or LS 301. These courses are regularly taught in the fall and spring semesters. View Details Bookmark Previous 1 2 3 4 5 6 Next University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
