ergraduate and graduate teaching in areas of mechanical engineering, mechanical engineering technology or industrial engineering related to the applicant’s strengths. Other responsibilities include advising and mentoring undergraduate students, participation in accreditation activities and com... View Details Bookmark Director of Budget and Finance STAFF - VA - 27047 University Health Partners SWC AVP OPs Staff Montana State University Student Wellness is seeking a Director of Budget and Finance to provide strategic leadership in financial planning and budget management for Student Wellness units including Campus Recreation, Counseling and Psychological Services, Student Health Services, and the broader SW enterprise. They will serve as the financial expert within Student Wellness, advising unit leads... View Details Bookmark Civil Engineering Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26083 College of Engineering Civil Engineering Faculty Civil Engineering faculty members contribute to excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching, advise and mentor undergraduate students, participate in college activities and committee assignments, and provide service to the University, State, and profession.The Civil Engineering Department is seeking professionals to serve as Instructors in the following areas:Basic Civil/Construction Engi... View Details Bookmark Pharmacy Technician STAFF - VA - 26424 University Health Partners SWC Pharmacy Staff Join a mission-driven healthcare team dedicated to MSU student well-being. The SHS Pharmacy Technician plays a key role in delivering accurate, confidential, and accessible pharmacy services to MSU students from a state-of-the-art campus facility. View Details Bookmark Networking/Cyber Security Non-Tenure Track Faculty - Gallatin College (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26042 Gallatin College Gallatin College Faculty Gallatin College seeks non-tenure track faculty for the Networking/Cyber Security programs. View Details Bookmark Postdoctoral Researcher – Political Science and Systems Engineering STAFF - VA - 26364 College of Letters & Science Political Science Staff Join an interdisciplinary postdoctoral fellowship at Montana State University, in collaboration with engineering and political science faculty, to implement an existing research program defined in the DigiCARES strategic plan that advances justice-enhanced resilience in next-generation energy system digital twins. The position offers hands-on research using real-world utility data and community... View Details Bookmark Major Gifts Program Manager STAFF - VA - 27072 Museum of the Rockies Museum of the Rockies Staff The Major Gifts Program Manager at Museum of the Rockies is responsible for building, soliciting, and stewarding relationships with donors capable of making gifts of $10,000 or more. The position manages a portfolio of 70-100 donors and prospects, primarily in the Bozeman area, and is expected to meet fundraising goals that support the museum’s annual operations, capital projects, exhibitions, ... View Details Bookmark Japanese Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) FAC - VA - 26106 College of Letters & Science Modern Languages & Literature Faculty Department of Modern Languages and Literatures maintains an applicant pool for Non-Tenure Track Instructors in Japanese. Instructors typically teach 1 to 5 language classes per semester. All positions are pending adequate enrollment and funding. This advertisement is for an applicant pool. It does not indicate whether or not there are any current openings. Qualified candidates will be contacted... View Details Bookmark Previous 1 2 3 4 5 6 Next University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data