    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52835": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Custodian I - Part-Time - Pool Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Custodian I - Part-Time - Pool Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please address the qualifications as you build your application and profile or you can attach a resume/cover letter. Questions? Contact: Search Support at auxjobs@montana.edu or 406-994-6468. Position Details Position Information Announcement Number STAFF - VA - 27083 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Search Support at auxjobs@montana.edu or 406-994-6468. Classification Title Custodian I - BZ Working Title Custodian I - Part-Time - Pool Brief Position Overview Residence Life Custodians provide cleaning and light maintenance services for the residence halls and associated areas. This part-time position is for up to 16hours per week. Position Number 4N0188, 4N0065 Department Residence Life Administration Division Auxiliary Services Appointment Type Classified Contract Term Fiscal Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Non-Exempt Union Affiliation Exempt from Collective Bargaining FTE .375 Benefits Eligible Not Eligible Salary $23.05 per hour Contract Type Classified Hourly If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement University Student Housing ( USH ) at MSU , offers a unique, on-campus living experience for students and their families as they focus on their academic success. Managing 18 active on-campus communities (Residence Halls and Apartments) which are the home of up to 6,500 residents. The departmental mission includes provision of reasonably priced living environments which are clean, attractive, well-maintained, comfortable, and include safety features; ensures the orderly and effective administration of the program through efficient management; and provides a learning environment and related co-curricular programs which promote maturity and academic success. Duties and Responsibilities Custodians provide cleaning and light maintenance services for the residence halls, student apartments, and associated areas. Custodians may work individually or on a team. This position is asked to interact in a professional and positive manner with students, tenants, and summer conferencing guests to accomplish the department mission and aid in retention. The primary emphasis is on: Cleaning public areas which include restrooms, laundry areas, stairwells etc Carpeted and hard-surface floor care Trash removal Set up and tear down of areas such as residence hall rooms/office spaces/public spaces dependent on department Other related custodial duties Actively participates as part of the team while performing other duties in support of the department’s mission. This is a part-time permanent position. Part-time employees work up to 16 hours a week and are eligible to receive holiday pay and annual & sick leave pay on a prorated basis. If you are a student of MSU and seek a student worker position, please go to: http://www.montana.edu/comeworkwithus/ . The University Student Housing Department lacks the necessary funding to provide sponsorship at this time. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Experience working in custodial, janitorial, housekeeping, etc. Experience working effectively with minimal or no supervision. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Experience providing excellent customer service. Experience operating floor scrubbers, extractors, or similar janitorial equipment. Certifications, classes completed, or knowledge of safety procedures utilized in a custodial, janitorial or housekeeping position. The Successful Candidate Will Positively and professionally perform all the functions of the position. Consistently exercise initiative and good judgment. Effectively and safely operate work-related equipment and tools. Accurately follow written and oral instructions and procedures. Exhibit strong communication skills. Work effectively and efficiently in close cooperation with staff in a team-oriented environment. Be able to complete multiple tasks in a timely manner. Quickly adapt to changing priorities. Possess strong organizational skills. Maintain excellent customer service. Be highly motivated and work with minimal supervision. Have excellent attention to detail. Represent the department and MSU to others in a professional and courteous manner. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements, but a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. This is a 12 month, permanent part-time, non-benefited position. Hours are up to 16 hours/week. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Stationary or moving about for extended periods of time Frequently moving, transporting and placing containers/objects up to 30 lbs, and occasionally up to 100 lbs. (items may include stacking chairs, folding tables, floor sealer, bed frames, dressers, desks, etc.) Moving up and down stairs occasionally while carrying containers/objects Moving up and down a step ladder Bending, kneeling, stretching and general moving about while stocking products Gripping handles on equipment Performing repetitive motions related to job duties Regular exposure to cleaning solutions Occasionally shovel snow This position has supervisory duties? No Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies Multiple Desired Start Date Upon completion of a successful search. Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Review of applications will be on a continual basis and will continue until the position is filled Special Instructions Please address the qualifications as you build your application and profile or you can attach a resume/cover letter. Questions? Contact: Search Support at auxjobs@montana.edu or 406-994-6468. EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
