    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52828": {
      "title": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Research Associate - Field Research Program",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Research Associate - Field Research Program Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Research Associate - Field Research Program Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is not eligible for new sponsorship. Position Details Position Information Announcement Number STAFF - VA - 27082 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Frankie Crutcher frankie.crutcher@montana.edu 406-994-2227 Classification Title Research Professional Working Title Research Associate - Field Research Program Brief Position Overview This position will work under the supervision of the Associate Professor of Plant Pathology at the Eastern Agricultural Research Center to manage and conduct field research projects focused on crop disease management and agricultural production systems. Responsibilities include establishing and maintaining research plots, collecting field data, managing research activities, performing data analysis, preparing reports and manuscripts, and supervising seasonal employees and student workers. This position provides an excellent opportunity for an early-career scientist to develop advanced skills in applied agricultural research, including field experiment management, research data collection and analysis, scientific communication, and supervision of research personnel. The successful candidate will gain experience working across a diverse portfolio of grant-funded research projects while contributing to research outcomes that support agricultural production in the Northern Great Plains. The successful candidate will be an experienced field researcher who enjoys hands-on agricultural research, working outdoors, and being part of a small collaborative research team within a rural agricultural community. This position requires flexibility, attention to detail, problem-solving skills, and a willingness to work together with other team members to successfully complete research objectives. Position Number 4C1473 Department AES EARC Division College of Agriculture/MAES Appointment Type Research Professional Contract Term Fiscal Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Exempt Union Affiliation Exempt from Collective Bargaining FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary Salary commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications. Contract Type LOA If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement This position provides scientific support for diverse applied agricultural research projects conducted by the Plant Pathology Program at the Eastern Agricultural Research Center. The Research Associate will play an important role in implementing field research projects, maintaining high-quality research standards, managing experimental data, supporting graduate student research, and communicating research findings through reports, presentations, and scientific publications. The position provides opportunities to develop expertise in field research management, experimental design, data analysis, scientific communication, and research project coordination while working as part of a collaborative research team. Duties and Responsibilities Conduct and coordinate field research activities, including plot establishment, maintenance, field evaluations, sampling, and harvest activities. Collect, organize, manage, and analyze research data using established protocols. Assist with experimental design, statistical analysis, and interpretation of research results. Maintain accurate records of research activities, field conditions, and project outcomes. Supervise and train research assistants, student employees, and temporary workers. Provide mentorship to graduate students. Lead in the preparation of technical reports, presentations, and scientific manuscripts. Operate research equipment, agricultural equipment, and university vehicles as needed. Assist with field days, research tours, and other outreach activities. Follow university safety policies and maintain a safe working environment. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Master’s degree in Plant Pathology, Crop Science, Agronomy, Agricultural Science, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated experience conducting hands-on agricultural field research including establishing, maintaining, evaluating, and harvesting research experiments. Experience in experimental design as well as collecting, managing, and analyzing scientific data. Experience using Microsoft Office and statistical software, including R or similar statistical programs. Ability to manage multiple projects and priorities. Effective written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively as part of a collaborative team. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Experience evaluating crop diseases or other agronomic traits. Demonstrated experience preparing scientific manuscripts, technical reports, or research presentations. Experience supervising students, research assistants, or temporary employees. Experience operating agricultural equipment and maintaining field research plots. Hands-on experience operating a backpack sprayer and applying experimental fungicides. The Successful Candidate Will Demonstrate enthusiasm and willingness to conduct hands-on agricultural field research. Work effectively as part of a collaborative team where members contribute to shared research goals. Take ownership of assigned responsibilities and complete tasks reliably with appropriate independence. Adapt to changing field conditions, weather, and research priorities. Maintain attention to detail when conducting experiments and collecting data. Communicate effectively with researchers, students, technicians, and collaborators. Demonstrate reliability, organization, professionalism, and good judgment. Develop and apply new skills in field research management, data analysis, scientific communication, and research coordination. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information Must possess or have the ability to obtain a valid Montana driver’s license within 3 months of hire. Ability to safely operate a pickup truck on highways, gravel roads, and agricultural field roads. Must obtain a Montana pesticide applicator license within 3 months of hire. Occasional evening, weekend, and extended-hour work may be required during planting, field evaluations, and harvest periods. Occasional overnight travel may be required for research activities, meetings, and conferences. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations: Move up to 40 pounds. Walk and stand for extended periods on uneven agricultural terrain. Bend, kneel, crouch, and reach while conducting field research activities. Safely operate university vehicles. Work outdoors for extended periods in varying weather conditions, including heat, cold, wind, dust, and precipitation. Work with and around pesticides, plant materials, and agricultural environments while using required personal protective equipment. This position has supervisory duties? Yes Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Screening of applications will begin on September 17, 2026 ; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions This position is not eligible for new sponsorship. EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
