    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52783": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Equipment Operator II Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Equipment Operator II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is not eligible for sponsorship. Position Details Position Information Announcement Number STAFF - VA - 27043 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Amber Gregg amber.gregg1@montana.edu 406-994-5454 Classification Title Equip Oper II Working Title Equipment Operator II Brief Position Overview The individual in this position will be a key player on the MSU Grounds/Waste team. Primarily focusing on waste, recycling and snow removal, this team player will complete a wide variety of duties in a great work environment. Position Number 4N0177 Department Facility Services Division University Services Appointment Type Classified Contract Term Fiscal Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Non-Exempt Union Affiliation Teamsters FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary Minimum $32.00 per hour, commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications Contract Type Classified Hourly If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement The Landscape and Grounds Department of Facilities Services is responsible for: Minimizing the deterioration of campus grounds Maintaining campus aesthetics Implementing campus landscape and grounds improvements Operating the recycling and waste programs Producing and reviewing plans and specifications for proposed construction projects, as well as evaluating and inspecting finished product of construction contractors Keeping the grounds free from physical hazards to campus users Duties and Responsibilities Under the general supervision of the Landscape and Grounds Manager, the individual in this position will operate a wide variety of specialized waste, grounds maintenance and snow removal equipment. Duties may include but are not limited to: Waste/ Recycling collection, loading, hauling and disposal Street, sidewalk and entryway snow removal and ice remediation Street and sidewalk maintenance Outdoor environmental safety Equipment maintenance Record keeping Performing other related duties as required Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills High School diploma or GED Valid Montana CDL – Minimum Class B Type II Experience in general commercial grounds or waste operations Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Operation of front-loading compactor garbage truck Commercial snow removal experience Experience maintaining specialized waste/grounds equipment The Successful Candidate Will Consistently exercise initiative and good judgment. Effectively and safely operate work-related equipment and tools. Accurately follow written and oral instructions and procedures. Communicate effectively with co-workers, supervisors, and clients in person, by phone, or electronically. Establish and maintain effective working relationships with supervisors, coworkers, and the public and be a successful team player. Provide excellent customer service; and represent the department and MSU to others in a professional and courteous manner. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information The work schedule varies seasonally and is highly weather dependent. The department utilizes split shifts to ensure winter snow coverage- typical available shifts are Monday- Friday 5:30 AM- 2:00PM or 8:30AM – 5:00PM. The person in this position may be called in for work at any time, particularly during the snow season. Weekend and holiday work may be required. The final candidate selected for this position will be required to successfully pass a pre-employment drug test. Upon providing proof of a valid Commercial Driver’s License ( CDL ) the person in this position will be enrolled in the random drug and alcohol testing program. The final candidate selected for this position will be required to successfully pass a background check. This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements, but a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s right to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodation. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Performing physically demanding work such as shoveling, ice chipping, post pounding etc. Personally move objects weighing up to 100 pounds, working in dirty and dusty conditions, as well as inclement weather. Receive and maintain valid Montana CDL Medical Certificate This position has supervisory duties? No Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Upon completion of a successful search Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Screening of applications will begin on August 17, 2026 ; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions This position is not eligible for sponsorship. EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
