    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52777": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Lead Systems Analyst Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Lead Systems Analyst Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Announcement Number STAFF - VA - 27055 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Nathan Fromelt nathan.fromelt@montana.edu 406-994-5181 Classification Title Computer Sys Analyst III Working Title Lead Systems Analyst Brief Position Overview Lead the Enterprise Service Group ( ESG ) Finance team to support the four-campus Banner Finance operations. Collaborate with business counterparts to establish project priorities, address reported issues, and maintain existing processes. Position Number 4M0954 Department UIT Enterprise Services Group CUF Division VP for Information Technology Appointment Type Classified Contract Term Fiscal Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Exempt Union Affiliation Exempt from Collective Bargaining FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary Salary range of $70,000 to $98,000 annually, commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications Contract Type Classified Hourly If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement In support of the Montana State University mission, University Information Technology ( UIT ) promotes, develops, delivers, and facilitates the use of information technology services and resources. The Enterprise Services Group is responsible for technical support of all major computer-based administrative applications for the four-campus MSU system. MSU uses Ellucian Banner software , running on an Oracle database, for the majority of its administrative tasks. Primary modules include Human Resources , Finance, Student, and Financial Aid. Duties and Responsibilities Under the supervision of the Director of Enterprise Services, the Lead Systems Analyst performs professional level work implementing and supporting the on-going operations for the EllucianBanner information system and for related custom applications and workflows used with the Finance information systems across the four-campuses of Montana State University. . The Banner Finance Lead Systems Analyst will: Supervise the day-to-day operations of the ESG -Finance team Collaborate directly with the Finance business counterparts to identify priority development and support efforts for Finance information systems across MSU campuses Foster positive and effective working relationships Provide systems analysis including assessing user requirements, analyzing alternatives, designing preferred solutions, specifying technical requirements, developing software modules, implementing solutions, and maintaining major software systems Manage projects and tasks associated with development and maintenance efforts Coordinate technical problem resolution Participate in joint efforts with other Banner teams and committees that interface or interact with Banner Finance systems. Serve on other university committees providing leadership and technical counsel. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Bachelor’s degree in computer science or related field, plus recent directly related experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Successful experience analyzing, designing, specifying, developing, programming, enhancing, and implementing complex administrative application systems that use relational database management systems and transaction processing techniques. Demonstrated ability to foster and maintain effective working relationships with varied constituents using appropriate interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated understanding of, and current intermediate or expert experience in applications programming with an emphasis on SQL , PL/ SQL , and/or database driven programming with modern software development tools. Successful experience managing multiple projects, prioritizing user requests, and delegating tasks to team members. Successful experience hiring, training, supervising, and mentoring technical staff. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Experience with university ERP systems (Ellucian Banner preferred). Experience with design, development, and deployment of integration components. Experience with design, development, deployment, and maintenance of applications employing ORACLE enterprise-wide relational database management systems, SQL , PL/ SQL , or other modern software architecture. Experience using reporting development tools. The Successful Candidate Will Possess exceptional interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills, including the ability to clearly explain technical information to a non-technical audience. Manage multiple projects and deadlines simultaneously, effectively prioritize competing demands, and facilitate the work of others using effective time and project management skills. Demonstrate leadership and excellent conflict management skills. Consistently exercise initiative and good judgment. Establish and maintain effective working relations with co-workers and the public in a team-oriented environment. Demonstrate commitment to service excellence with the ability to collaborate with and view processes and products from the lens of constituents/end users. Physical Demands Maintain confidentiality of records and information. Demonstrate ability to represent MSU and University Information Technology ( UIT ) and its programs to others in a professional and courteous manner. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information This position is not eligible for sponsorship. This is a full-time, on-site position based at our Bozeman, Montana campus. Occasional travel will be required. This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements, but a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed in this description are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. This position has supervisory duties? Yes Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Upon completion of a successful search Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Screening of applications will begin on August 31, 2026 ; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
