    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52765": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Custodial Supervisor II Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Custodial Supervisor II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is not eligible for new sponsorship. Please address the qualifications in your cover letter and resume. Questions? Contact: Search Support at auxjobs@montana.edu or 406-994-6468. Position Details Position Information Announcement Number STAFF - VA - 27074 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Search Support at auxjobs@montana.edu or 406-994-6468 Classification Title Custodial Supv II - BZ Working Title Custodial Supervisor II Brief Position Overview Position Number 4N0057 Department Residence Life Administration Division Auxiliary Services Appointment Type Classified Contract Term Fiscal Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Non-Exempt Union Affiliation Exempt from Collective Bargaining FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary $35.48 per hour Contract Type Classified Hourly If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement University Student Housing manages 18 active on-campus communities (11 Residence Halls and 7 Apartments) which are the home of up to 6,500 residents . The Residence Life Custodial Team provides cleaning and maintenance services in and around the residence halls and associated areas. The primary emphasis is on cleaning the public areas which include restrooms, carpeted and hard-surface floor care, trash removal, room set-ups and other related duties. Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Associate Director of Building Services, the Custodial Supervisor II ensures the on-site supervision and coordination of custodial activities for the residence life buildings and their associated areas. This working manager position has duties including: Actively supervises and directs the work of the custodial crew to ensure excellent customer service to students and building patrons. Directly supervises 2 Custodial Supervisor Is and indirectly supervises the custodian team (84 during AY and up to 115 during breaks). The team is comprised of Custodians IIs, Custodian Is, student and summer/winter break staff. They lead and guide the hiring, training, performance evaluation, payroll, etc for the crew. Provides and schedules ongoing professional development and training opportunities for the custodial team on equipment, industry standards, team development, and other topics as they arise. Monitors staffing levels, attendance, and operational needs and adjusts assignments and resources to maintain effective coverage across assigned residence halls. Oversees and directs the operational activities of the custodial team to ensure assignments are completed in a safe, effective, and efficient manner. Ensures safety and security of students, building patrons and staff. Maintains budgetary goals and expectations. Maintains a working knowledge of all equipment and infrastructure necessary to clean and maintain dense population housing facilities and associated areas. Performs regular inspections of grounds and facilities to determine cleaning needs and repairs. Oversees and maintains departmental standard operating procedures and conducts regular quality inspections. Available to troubleshoot and solve building/facility issues. Oversees all pest control efforts. Maintains the yearly cleaning calendar, scheduling deep cleaning and special maintenance projects to not conflict with academic year and summer conferencing. Manages the custodial equipment and inventory program to meet budget goals to include: Performs all duties related to purchasing chemicals and equipment while maintaining compliance with MSU’s purchasing guidelines and policies. Develops and implements the short- and long-term equipment replacement plans. Ensures chemicals and supplies are properly stored, labeled, and managed in accordance with applicable safety requirements and departmental procedures. Collaborates regularly with partners across campus in Facilities Management, Sustainability, Culinary Services, Procurement, and various Auxiliary Services offices. Researches industry innovations and forecasts needs of facilities and users. Works as part of the management team on short and long range planning. Performs a variety of administrative tasks in support of the department (abandon property process and follow up, ad-hoc reporting, payroll, creation and maintenance of standard operating procedures, work orders, overtime memos, assignments and schedules, etc.) Oversees the custodial emergency over-time call out list and acts as a “custodian on call” as needed. And actively participates as part of the team while performing other duties in support of the department’s mission. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Substantial experience supervising custodial and/or light maintenance activities in a commercial, institutional, high density housing, or similar setting or an equivalent combination of relevant education and experience. Demonstrated experience managing a diverse group of personnel including full and part-time, temporary, and/or college aged employees. Proficient experience using computers and various software packages. Demonstrated knowledge of safety procedures utilized while conducting custodial work. Extensive customer service experience dealing effectively and diplomatically with a variety of people. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Certifications/Classes related to custodial, sanitation, building maintenance etc. Experience with inventory control. Experience enforcing building and security regulations. The Successful Candidate Will Exude enthusiasm and have a high level of integrity and customer orientation while interacting with a wide range of individuals from staff to students to parents and vendors. Sensitive to the needs of patrons and have an extensive knowledge of customer service. Maintain current knowledge of the cleaning industry. Maintain composure while working with a broad spectrum of personalities under stress, pressure, and time sensitive demands of the job. Possess solid problem solving skills. Exhibit leadership and team building skills. Be self-motivated, adapt to frequently changing priorities, and able to organize and prioritize multiple work assignments and meet deadlines. Exercise good judgment and make consistent decisions. Be able to operate and maintain departmental equipment. Represent University Student Housing and its programs in a positive, professional courteous manner. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements, but a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Must possess currently or be eligible to obtain a valid State of Montana Driver’s license and have an acceptable driving record (less than 12 points). Do NOT send a copy of the driver’s license. If the successful candidate possesses a valid out of state driver’s license, candidate must obtain a valid Montana driver’s license within 60 days. Occasionally work evenings, weekends, long hours, consecutive days during busy periods, and occasional holidays as the school and event schedule demands. Will manage the custodial over-time call out list and occasionally be in an after hours response status for immediate situations as needed. Occasionally work outside and in inclement weather. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Required to wear safety gear as needed. Regular exposure to cleaning solutions. Routinely transport and place items weighing up to 50+ lbs, and occasionally up to 100lbs. Move about or traverse grounds and facilities for long periods of time. Occasionally perform cleaning duties; grip handles on cleaning equipment; ascend/descend stairs and step ladders; and be comfortable working at heights. Occasionally shovel snow. This position has supervisory duties? Yes Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Upon completion of a successful search. Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Screening of applications will begin on September 14, 2026 ; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions This position is not eligible for new sponsorship. Please address the qualifications in your cover letter and resume. Questions? Contact: Search Support at auxjobs@montana.edu or 406-994-6468. EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
